1
00:00:00,395 --> 00:00:02,333
Just a one-point difference now.

2
00:00:03,780 --> 00:00:05,047
Let's go!

3
00:00:05,048 --> 00:00:08,007
(It's neck and neck,
just a one-point difference.)

4
00:00:08,485 --> 00:00:12,388
(They need to keep the lead.)

5
00:00:12,389 --> 00:00:14,957
Enkhsoyol, hit it deep if you're not sure.

6
00:00:15,091 --> 00:00:16,992
- Don't hit the net and go deep.
- Okay.

7
00:00:17,854 --> 00:00:21,190
Na Hyeon, drop back and cover Enkhsoyol.

8
00:00:21,798 --> 00:00:23,966
Hey, Eun Jin. I'm dropping back.

9
00:00:23,967 --> 00:00:25,501
Watch out for the short serve.

10
00:00:25,502 --> 00:00:26,435
(Marked player, Enkhsoyol)

11
00:00:26,603 --> 00:00:27,403
Just hit it.

12
00:00:29,339 --> 00:00:30,472
(Nice receive!)

13
00:00:31,408 --> 00:00:33,008
Hit it deep! Deep!

14
00:00:33,310 --> 00:00:35,144
(Hit it deep.)

15
00:00:35,378 --> 00:00:36,311
One, two!

16
00:00:37,781 --> 00:00:39,248
- That's it!
- Nice!

17
00:00:39,249 --> 00:00:41,250
That was a very nice spike.

18
00:00:41,251 --> 00:00:44,420
Enkhsoyol is attacking with confidence...

19
00:00:44,421 --> 00:00:46,822
and powerful footwork in this game.

20
00:00:46,823 --> 00:00:47,556
That's right.

21
00:00:49,317 --> 00:00:51,351
(Satisfied)

22
00:00:53,722 --> 00:00:54,855
(Na Hee's serve)

23
00:00:54,856 --> 00:00:55,989
Na Hee serves.

24
00:00:59,494 --> 00:01:01,094
They're hitting it long. Spike!

25
00:01:01,196 --> 00:01:02,163
(Na Hee's diving dig)

26
00:01:02,397 --> 00:01:03,263
Jin!

27
00:01:06,468 --> 00:01:07,268
Wait!

28
00:01:07,269 --> 00:01:09,170
- Point won!
- Yes.

29
00:01:09,170 --> 00:01:12,305
Jin's a setter, but she also has power.

30
00:01:12,474 --> 00:01:13,374
Nice!

31
00:01:13,776 --> 00:01:15,009
Seriously, nice!

32
00:01:15,977 --> 00:01:16,810
Timeout.

33
00:01:16,811 --> 00:01:20,339
(Timeout call)

34
00:01:22,029 --> 00:01:25,286
Kwangju Women's University's
first timeout.

35
00:01:25,787 --> 00:01:28,522
Come on. Don't play it safe on defense.

36
00:01:28,523 --> 00:01:30,858
- You think you're a psychic?
- No.

37
00:01:30,859 --> 00:01:32,593
Can you tell where they're going to hit?

38
00:01:32,594 --> 00:01:33,527
No, coach.

39
00:01:34,829 --> 00:01:37,097
(Libero's previous Pre-emptive play)

40
00:01:37,098 --> 00:01:39,566
I told you to never stop moving
during the game!

41
00:01:39,567 --> 00:01:40,700
- Yes.
- Don't just stand there.

42
00:01:40,702 --> 00:01:42,703
Keep moving your feet, manage your speed,

43
00:01:42,704 --> 00:01:44,371
and look for the right timing!

44
00:01:44,372 --> 00:01:46,106
- But you just stood there!
- Sorry, coach.

45
00:01:46,841 --> 00:01:49,576
(Getting intense)

46
00:01:50,378 --> 00:01:52,346
They're going to play tips
when there's an opportunity...

47
00:01:52,347 --> 00:01:54,448
so make a quick decision and defend it!

48
00:01:54,449 --> 00:01:56,016
- Yes, coach.
- Let's go, guys.

49
00:01:56,017 --> 00:01:57,017
- Let's go!
- Yes!

50
00:01:57,018 --> 00:01:58,352
(Let's do this,
Kwangju Women's University!)

51
00:01:58,353 --> 00:02:00,521
- Let's go, guys!
- Yes, let's go!

52
00:02:02,424 --> 00:02:05,292
Hyeon Jeong, track the setter's movement.

53
00:02:05,560 --> 00:02:06,393
Yes, coach.

54
00:02:07,196 --> 00:02:08,963
It's 16 to 18, a two-point difference.

55
00:02:10,031 --> 00:02:11,565
Just serve in the middle.

56
00:02:11,666 --> 00:02:13,967
(Understood.)

57
00:02:16,404 --> 00:02:18,338
- They barely received it!
- Yes, nice!

58
00:02:19,274 --> 00:02:20,174
Watch out!

59
00:02:20,642 --> 00:02:21,642
That's it!

60
00:02:21,643 --> 00:02:22,676
Spike!

61
00:02:23,044 --> 00:02:24,378
They saved it.

62
00:02:24,846 --> 00:02:26,613
(Rushing in and push shot.)

63
00:02:26,614 --> 00:02:28,615
- Remember the tactic!
- They barely got it through.

64
00:02:28,616 --> 00:02:30,050
It's a chance to strike back!

65
00:02:30,352 --> 00:02:31,619
(No way.)

66
00:02:31,619 --> 00:02:33,620
- It's blocked!
- Hit it deep!

67
00:02:33,621 --> 00:02:36,022
It's a free ball. They have to score this.

68
00:02:36,024 --> 00:02:37,458
Yes, they have to score this.

69
00:02:37,459 --> 00:02:38,526
(This is a golden opportunity.)

70
00:02:39,561 --> 00:02:40,628
Back toss.

71
00:02:40,628 --> 00:02:41,461
(Whose ball is it?)

72
00:02:41,463 --> 00:02:42,463
(It's Enkhsoyol's.)

73
00:02:42,464 --> 00:02:44,865
One, two!

74
00:02:46,902 --> 00:02:48,035
Spike!

75
00:02:48,036 --> 00:02:49,203
(They blocked it!)

76
00:02:51,907 --> 00:02:53,407
They pushed it over!

77
00:02:54,809 --> 00:02:55,609
Back toss!

78
00:02:55,978 --> 00:02:57,445
Spike from the right.

79
00:02:57,913 --> 00:02:59,714
Seung Ju saved the ball.
Jin's stepping in.

80
00:02:59,714 --> 00:03:00,581
Push it over!

81
00:03:01,216 --> 00:03:02,316
Spike!

82
00:03:03,084 --> 00:03:04,084
It's back again.

83
00:03:04,819 --> 00:03:06,019
Another attack!

84
00:03:06,521 --> 00:03:07,621
Spike!

85
00:03:08,223 --> 00:03:10,658
(The ball goes to the setter.)

86
00:03:11,293 --> 00:03:13,694
(Watch the setter's movement...)

87
00:03:14,129 --> 00:03:15,930
(and block it!)

88
00:03:17,465 --> 00:03:20,200
Point from a block!

89
00:03:20,735 --> 00:03:22,736
That was a very important point.

90
00:03:22,737 --> 00:03:24,104
(First set, 16 to 19)

91
00:03:25,440 --> 00:03:28,542
(She watched the setter closely
and scored on a block.)

92
00:03:28,543 --> 00:03:32,112
They finished off a mega rally
with a fantastic block.

93
00:03:33,181 --> 00:03:34,782
(The game continues.)

94
00:03:36,418 --> 00:03:37,985
(Captain Pyo's spike)

95
00:03:37,986 --> 00:03:38,919
No!

96
00:03:39,254 --> 00:03:41,088
(You can seriously...)

97
00:03:41,089 --> 00:03:42,590
(save this?)

98
00:03:42,590 --> 00:03:44,724
(They failed!)

99
00:03:45,760 --> 00:03:47,728
(First set, Kwangju Women's University 17
: Wonder Dogs 21)

100
00:03:47,863 --> 00:03:51,231
Come on! Let's just get one right!
Watch the ball!

101
00:03:51,366 --> 00:03:53,334
Stay focused. We'll get our chance.

102
00:03:53,735 --> 00:03:55,202
(An intense rally)

103
00:03:55,570 --> 00:03:56,970
One, two. Spike coming!

104
00:03:56,971 --> 00:03:58,305
(Captain Pyo is...)

105
00:03:58,306 --> 00:03:59,706
(attacking again!)

106
00:03:59,908 --> 00:04:00,875
Go! Save it!

107
00:04:01,609 --> 00:04:02,876
It's a four-point difference now.

108
00:04:03,078 --> 00:04:05,479
(First set, Kwangju Women's University 18
: Wonder Dogs 23)

109
00:04:05,480 --> 00:04:07,581
- She's our ace for a reason.
- Yes.

110
00:04:07,582 --> 00:04:11,519
The momentum has shifted
after the last blocking point...

111
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:13,353
and they're taking the lead now.

112
00:04:14,322 --> 00:04:15,422
Watch their movements!

113
00:04:16,491 --> 00:04:17,791
(Firing up)

114
00:04:17,792 --> 00:04:19,226
One step in!

115
00:04:19,661 --> 00:04:20,427
Song Hee!

116
00:04:20,428 --> 00:04:22,095
- Don't serve to libero.
- Okay.

117
00:04:22,263 --> 00:04:24,030
Don't serve to libero!

118
00:04:24,032 --> 00:04:27,067
(Ordering to avoid serving the ball
toward the libero)

119
00:04:27,402 --> 00:04:29,536
(Not to where the libero is)

120
00:04:30,005 --> 00:04:30,905
Song Hee.

121
00:04:30,905 --> 00:04:32,606
(Song Hee serving)

122
00:04:33,274 --> 00:04:34,274
Not in that way!

123
00:04:34,542 --> 00:04:35,509
One, two!

124
00:04:36,244 --> 00:04:37,311
(Straight to the libero)

125
00:04:37,312 --> 00:04:38,846
(She served it right
to the libero's face.)

126
00:04:39,714 --> 00:04:40,547
A fake pass.

127
00:04:41,016 --> 00:04:41,882
They saved it.

128
00:04:42,283 --> 00:04:43,183
Back step.

129
00:04:43,818 --> 00:04:45,285
Pushing it with power!

130
00:04:46,121 --> 00:04:47,321
The ball is coming back.

131
00:04:47,856 --> 00:04:48,856
Hye In passes.

132
00:04:49,358 --> 00:04:50,457
Set it up.

133
00:04:50,458 --> 00:04:51,591
(A very nice...)

134
00:04:51,593 --> 00:04:52,493
(fast attack)

135
00:04:53,462 --> 00:04:54,461
Na Hee's attack.

136
00:04:54,629 --> 00:04:57,331
Won​​der Dogs are at set point.

137
00:04:58,033 --> 00:05:00,501
(One more point to win the first set)

138
00:05:00,502 --> 00:05:02,336
Set point of the first set.

139
00:05:02,337 --> 00:05:04,905
(Wonder Dogs' set point)

140
00:05:05,373 --> 00:05:07,040
(They have to win this.)

141
00:05:07,041 --> 00:05:07,908
(Glancing)

142
00:05:08,510 --> 00:05:09,410
(Deep breath)

143
00:05:09,410 --> 00:05:10,477
Serve!

144
00:05:10,478 --> 00:05:13,213
(Once again, Song Hee serves)

145
00:05:15,717 --> 00:05:16,817
It's out!

146
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:20,153
Sorry.

147
00:05:21,122 --> 00:05:24,891
(Serving error
at a crucial set point moment)

148
00:05:25,126 --> 00:05:26,693
What is up with you?

149
00:05:29,164 --> 00:05:30,264
Are you kidding me?

150
00:05:30,432 --> 00:05:33,100
(There's a reason
Coach Yeon Koung is so mad.)

151
00:05:36,237 --> 00:05:38,705
(Previous Enkhsoyol's serving error)

152
00:05:38,706 --> 00:05:40,407
What did I tell you, Enkhsoyol?

153
00:05:40,842 --> 00:05:42,176
- In between.
- No, hit it deep.

154
00:05:42,177 --> 00:05:45,513
- Right, deep.
- That's not your play. Hit it deep.

155
00:05:48,216 --> 00:05:49,183
Darn it.

156
00:05:49,184 --> 00:05:50,718
(And then, Hyeon Jeong's serving error)

157
00:05:51,352 --> 00:05:55,021
(Getting upset)

158
00:05:55,256 --> 00:05:56,890
We already made two mistakes.

159
00:05:56,958 --> 00:05:58,392
- Do you know what they were?
- Serving errors.

160
00:05:58,827 --> 00:06:00,127
It was neither fast,

161
00:06:00,128 --> 00:06:02,529
nor aimed right in between.

162
00:06:03,198 --> 00:06:06,534
(Getting furious
for not following the agreed tactic)

163
00:06:07,068 --> 00:06:11,104
I have a feeling they'll train hard
for serving after today's game.

164
00:06:11,272 --> 00:06:13,940
What the heck were they doing
during serve training?

165
00:06:16,644 --> 00:06:17,911
Come on, Yun Ah.

166
00:06:18,780 --> 00:06:19,646
I'm calling a substitute.

167
00:06:22,317 --> 00:06:24,418
Kwangju Women's University
player substitution.

168
00:06:24,419 --> 00:06:26,588
Number 9 in, number 17 out.

169
00:06:26,588 --> 00:06:28,455
Take it easy, Yun Ah.
Just serve and defend.

170
00:06:28,456 --> 00:06:29,389
Yes, coach.

171
00:06:29,891 --> 00:06:32,059
(A substitution only for the serves)

172
00:06:32,060 --> 00:06:33,594
Son Yun Ah is in.

173
00:06:33,595 --> 00:06:35,096
(Son Yun Ah, 2024 KUSF MVP award winner)

174
00:06:35,697 --> 00:06:37,798
(Tensing up)

175
00:06:37,799 --> 00:06:38,733
Short serve.

176
00:06:38,734 --> 00:06:39,967
Let's go!

177
00:06:39,968 --> 00:06:41,068
(Ace Yun Ah serving)

178
00:06:41,069 --> 00:06:42,336
It's 24 to 19.

179
00:06:43,004 --> 00:06:43,971
Nice serve.

180
00:06:44,539 --> 00:06:46,807
Point from serve, Yun Ah!

181
00:06:46,808 --> 00:06:48,876
(Kwangju Women's University's service ace)

182
00:06:51,379 --> 00:06:54,549
(Continuous mistakes on the set point)

183
00:06:54,550 --> 00:06:56,517
It looks like Coach Yeon Koung...

184
00:06:56,517 --> 00:06:58,651
is trying to hold it in right now.

185
00:06:58,987 --> 00:07:00,888
She's biting her tongue.

186
00:07:00,888 --> 00:07:01,988
She's holding it in.

187
00:07:01,990 --> 00:07:02,957
(She lost her words.)

188
00:07:03,358 --> 00:07:07,795
(Wonder Dogs look visibly uneasy)

189
00:07:09,063 --> 00:07:11,097
Too short. It's all too short.

190
00:07:13,067 --> 00:07:14,634
(They needed to hear that.)

191
00:07:16,304 --> 00:07:17,204
(Targeting Song Hee)

192
00:07:17,205 --> 00:07:18,338
Go to the left.

193
00:07:18,740 --> 00:07:19,808
It's 20 to 24.

194
00:07:19,808 --> 00:07:21,241
They can't drag this out any longer.

195
00:07:23,878 --> 00:07:25,045
It hit the net!

196
00:07:25,046 --> 00:07:27,814
(They barely passed the serve.)

197
00:07:28,650 --> 00:07:29,917
They pushed it over.

198
00:07:30,185 --> 00:07:31,785
Kwangju Women's University's free ball.

199
00:07:31,786 --> 00:07:34,021
They're passing as Coach Choi ordered.
- Hit it, quick!

200
00:07:34,022 --> 00:07:34,922
One, two!

201
00:07:36,157 --> 00:07:37,758
Blocked it on the left side.

202
00:07:39,427 --> 00:07:42,662
They finally have another chance to win!
What will they do?

203
00:07:44,799 --> 00:07:46,566
(The ball is set nicely.)

204
00:07:46,668 --> 00:07:48,335
(Seung Ju spikes!)

205
00:07:48,336 --> 00:07:50,938
Seung Ju spikes on the left side!

206
00:07:50,938 --> 00:07:53,173
They did a good play.

207
00:07:53,474 --> 00:07:56,876
(First set, Kwangju Women's University 20
: Wonder Dogs 25)

208
00:07:57,845 --> 00:07:59,445
It's 25 to 20.

209
00:07:59,447 --> 00:08:01,415
Wonder Dogs win the first set.

210
00:08:01,416 --> 00:08:03,183
(The rookie coach is still frustrated.)

211
00:08:03,651 --> 00:08:05,151
(Second set timeout)

212
00:08:05,153 --> 00:08:06,183
Get me the score sheet.

213
00:08:14,696 --> 00:08:17,965
We made 10 errors during the first set.

214
00:08:17,965 --> 00:08:19,199
Only 1 set, 10 errors.

215
00:08:23,504 --> 00:08:31,411
(They lost 10 points purely
due to errors during the first set.)

216
00:08:34,983 --> 00:08:38,218
Your serves was slow and off.

217
00:08:38,419 --> 00:08:40,620
You don't hit in between,
and they're slow.

218
00:08:40,788 --> 00:08:42,789
It was just completely off.

219
00:08:42,790 --> 00:08:43,723
- Yes, coach.
- Come on.

220
00:08:44,125 --> 00:08:47,227
Now we know their play style.

221
00:08:47,528 --> 00:08:49,128
We need to be more aggressive now.

222
00:08:49,130 --> 00:08:50,964
We weren't even playing aggressively,

223
00:08:50,965 --> 00:08:53,266
but you were still neck and neck.

224
00:08:53,267 --> 00:08:54,367
- Right?
- Yes.

225
00:08:54,736 --> 00:08:56,469
We can throw them off...

226
00:08:56,471 --> 00:08:57,905
if we push them hard.

227
00:08:57,905 --> 00:08:59,139
- Yes, coach.
- Yes, coach.

228
00:08:59,140 --> 00:09:00,774
- Go, Kwangju Women's University!
- Let's go!

229
00:09:00,775 --> 00:09:01,608
Let's do this!

230
00:09:02,877 --> 00:09:04,644
- One, two, three.
- Go, Kwangju Women's University!

231
00:09:04,645 --> 00:09:06,279
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

232
00:09:06,280 --> 00:09:08,081
(Full of energy)

233
00:09:08,683 --> 00:09:10,083
Let's do it right this time!

234
00:09:10,818 --> 00:09:14,354
They need to bring their A-game
for the second set.

235
00:09:14,762 --> 00:09:18,064
Yeon Hwa, you must make a definitive play!
Center yourself!

236
00:09:18,723 --> 00:09:20,190
Don't shake!

237
00:09:20,191 --> 00:09:21,591
(Which of the rookie coaches
will take the second set?)

238
00:09:21,793 --> 00:09:25,596
Song Hee replaced Chae Rim on the court.

239
00:09:25,797 --> 00:09:26,797
Let's go!

240
00:09:26,798 --> 00:09:28,465
(Second set, Kwangju Women's University 0
: Wonder Dogs 0)

241
00:09:29,034 --> 00:09:30,234
(A serve by Ah Hyeon)

242
00:09:30,235 --> 00:09:31,635
The second set begins now!

243
00:09:31,963 --> 00:09:33,491
Great!

244
00:09:33,685 --> 00:09:34,585
Mine!

245
00:09:35,614 --> 00:09:37,114
- Hit it!
- Song Hee!

246
00:09:37,116 --> 00:09:38,316
You've got this one!

247
00:09:39,251 --> 00:09:40,384
Hit it down the line!

248
00:09:40,386 --> 00:09:41,419
Hit it!

249
00:09:42,022 --> 00:09:42,854
Set it.

250
00:09:43,359 --> 00:09:44,826
(Block point)

251
00:09:44,827 --> 00:09:45,827
It's blocked!

252
00:09:46,262 --> 00:09:48,129
Yes!

253
00:09:48,330 --> 00:09:48,864
Good job.

254
00:09:48,888 --> 00:09:50,464
- Go, Wonder!
- Go, Wonder!

255
00:09:50,466 --> 00:09:51,466
That's right!

256
00:09:52,868 --> 00:09:54,302
Nice block!

257
00:09:56,172 --> 00:09:57,572
Nice block!

258
00:09:57,573 --> 00:09:59,574
Hyeon Jeong, I told you to stay there
because she'd get it.

259
00:09:59,575 --> 00:10:01,643
Focus on the center.
That's where you should be.

260
00:10:01,644 --> 00:10:03,278
Just block the balls coming in the middle.

261
00:10:03,279 --> 00:10:04,479
(Yeon Koung alone found the mistake.)

262
00:10:04,980 --> 00:10:07,215
(During the serve receive)

263
00:10:07,883 --> 00:10:09,484
(Song Hee was hesitating.)

264
00:10:10,653 --> 00:10:12,621
Why is she covering that area?

265
00:10:13,522 --> 00:10:15,656
(Even the process must be perfect.)

266
00:10:15,658 --> 00:10:16,591
The score is 1 to 0.

267
00:10:17,293 --> 00:10:18,593
(A serve by Enkhsoyol)

268
00:10:18,594 --> 00:10:19,527
The server is Enkhsoyol.

269
00:10:21,130 --> 00:10:21,963
Mine.

270
00:10:23,632 --> 00:10:25,099
The ball has a heavy spin.

271
00:10:26,435 --> 00:10:27,201
Yeon Hwa!

272
00:10:28,104 --> 00:10:30,138
Go get it! It's a chance.

273
00:10:30,340 --> 00:10:31,339
Under toss.

274
00:10:32,575 --> 00:10:33,775
Get ready for a feint move.

275
00:10:34,877 --> 00:10:36,144
(Sliding dig)

276
00:10:36,145 --> 00:10:37,979
- Once again.
- The chance has come.

277
00:10:37,980 --> 00:10:39,514
Go for it!

278
00:10:39,515 --> 00:10:41,049
Jin's back toss!

279
00:10:43,719 --> 00:10:44,752
The ball is blocked.

280
00:10:44,753 --> 00:10:46,520
(Toss error)

281
00:10:47,390 --> 00:10:49,958
After a successful dig,
Seung Ju jumps on the opposite side.

282
00:10:50,292 --> 00:10:51,726
(Not a chance.)

283
00:10:53,295 --> 00:10:54,429
(MVP Na Hyeon's spike)

284
00:10:54,430 --> 00:10:55,463
Spike.

285
00:10:55,898 --> 00:10:57,765
Hye In dug it. The ball is set.

286
00:10:59,001 --> 00:11:00,435
It's Seung Ju once again.

287
00:11:00,436 --> 00:11:03,138
- She hit it down the line!
- That was a clever choice.

288
00:11:03,172 --> 00:11:04,906
- That was great.
- You're doing fine.

289
00:11:05,841 --> 00:11:10,244
She just flicked her wrist
in that direction at the end.

290
00:11:10,479 --> 00:11:12,280
That was actually...

291
00:11:12,415 --> 00:11:15,951
- Coach Kim's specialty.
- Right. It's called a blind spike.

292
00:11:17,520 --> 00:11:19,087
- Okay!
- Good!

293
00:11:19,922 --> 00:11:21,155
Jin is rushing too much.

294
00:11:22,558 --> 00:11:24,626
They could only hit when she set the ball.

295
00:11:24,627 --> 00:11:26,094
(Only the rookie coach finds it not okay.)

296
00:11:26,328 --> 00:11:27,895
(And neither is he.)

297
00:11:27,897 --> 00:11:30,465
You should be covering,
reading the attack might come this way,

298
00:11:30,466 --> 00:11:31,399
but you're just standing there.

299
00:11:31,400 --> 00:11:34,235
Do you think she can score every point
all the time?

300
00:11:34,236 --> 00:11:35,403
- Okay!
- Okay!

301
00:11:37,339 --> 00:11:39,975
Jin, they can't hit the ball right.

302
00:11:40,409 --> 00:11:42,210
The tide can be turned around anytime,

303
00:11:42,211 --> 00:11:44,212
so the game management should be done
very sensitively.

304
00:11:45,214 --> 00:11:46,214
(Enkhsoyol's serve again)

305
00:11:46,215 --> 00:11:47,115
Serve!

306
00:11:49,585 --> 00:11:51,119
Oh, my gosh!

307
00:11:53,522 --> 00:11:56,057
(A service error)

308
00:11:58,494 --> 00:12:00,495
(Unbelievable.)

309
00:12:00,496 --> 00:12:02,095
- Make it short.
- Okay.

310
00:12:02,096 --> 00:12:04,699
(Small mistakes led to a big error.)

311
00:12:06,739 --> 00:12:09,741
(The opponent's error is our chance.)

312
00:12:09,909 --> 00:12:13,211
We'll stick to the second plan.

313
00:12:14,647 --> 00:12:16,881
Slow down. Good. Set it higher!

314
00:12:17,450 --> 00:12:18,350
Ye Jin!

315
00:12:18,684 --> 00:12:20,551
Spike!

316
00:12:21,487 --> 00:12:23,288
- That was a good attack.
- They scored a point!

317
00:12:23,289 --> 00:12:24,723
(Block out)

318
00:12:25,358 --> 00:12:29,661
(Go at their right side aggressively.)

319
00:12:30,163 --> 00:12:34,133
(And they went to attack the right side.)

320
00:12:34,434 --> 00:12:35,868
Slow down.

321
00:12:37,837 --> 00:12:40,272
Ye Jin, you're on fire today!

322
00:12:40,273 --> 00:12:42,074
(Kwangju Women's University's attack
caught Yeon Koung off guard.)

323
00:12:42,208 --> 00:12:44,476
Keep an eye on number 13.

324
00:12:44,744 --> 00:12:47,012
Ye Jin, great. Set it!

325
00:12:47,013 --> 00:12:48,480
Go for it!

326
00:12:48,481 --> 00:12:50,015
- Go!
- Open attack!

327
00:12:50,045 --> 00:12:52,433
(Ye Jin successfully attacked
the right side.)

328
00:12:55,157 --> 00:12:56,825
- Ye Jin, nice!
- Nice!

329
00:12:56,826 --> 00:12:59,160
Ye Jin, you now know how to attack, right?

330
00:12:59,228 --> 00:13:02,030
You're on a roll today.
Just hit it like that.

331
00:13:02,030 --> 00:13:03,197
Awesome!

332
00:13:04,333 --> 00:13:08,169
(They seem to have the momentum.)

333
00:13:08,170 --> 00:13:09,771
The score is 5 to 3.

334
00:13:10,643 --> 00:13:11,810
Let's go to number two. Seung Ju.

335
00:13:12,408 --> 00:13:13,308
Number two?

336
00:13:13,308 --> 00:13:15,376
(A targeted serve aimed at Seung Ju)

337
00:13:15,377 --> 00:13:16,911
That's it!

338
00:13:16,912 --> 00:13:17,912
She dives to make the reception.

339
00:13:17,913 --> 00:13:19,280
(The receive is shaking.)

340
00:13:19,715 --> 00:13:21,516
- Na Hyeon!
- It's a quick attack.

341
00:13:22,217 --> 00:13:23,217
In 1, 2!

342
00:13:23,685 --> 00:13:24,718
A moving attack!

343
00:13:24,719 --> 00:13:27,444
(They helplessly lose a point,
even knowing Wonderdogs' plan.)

344
00:13:27,446 --> 00:13:30,148
You should've waited
until the count of two,

345
00:13:30,149 --> 00:13:31,449
but you jumped too soon!

346
00:13:31,450 --> 00:13:32,483
Okay!

347
00:13:32,485 --> 00:13:33,552
Good.

348
00:13:33,553 --> 00:13:37,121
(Amid the invisible mind games
between the two coaches)

349
00:13:37,122 --> 00:13:38,356
The score is 7 to 3.

350
00:13:39,401 --> 00:13:42,270
All right. The opponent's play
has sped up.

351
00:13:42,295 --> 00:13:43,729
If the defenders are no-block,
what should we do?

352
00:13:43,729 --> 00:13:45,196
We need to move forward in defense.

353
00:13:45,198 --> 00:13:46,065
- Okay!
- Okay!

354
00:13:50,369 --> 00:13:52,003
Step by step!

355
00:13:53,539 --> 00:13:55,640
Relax! That's it. Nice save!

356
00:13:55,742 --> 00:13:56,775
Get in for coverage!

357
00:13:57,477 --> 00:13:58,310
(Forward in the front)

358
00:13:58,311 --> 00:13:59,912
They set the ball and hit it
to the middle.

359
00:14:02,683 --> 00:14:04,850
- It's C.
- Enkhsoyol, you know what to do!

360
00:14:11,691 --> 00:14:12,924
Enkhsoyol!

361
00:14:12,925 --> 00:14:14,459
- That was a nice attack.
- That was a brilliant hit.

362
00:14:15,762 --> 00:14:18,230
- It was speedy and precise.
- Enkhsoyol, nice job!

363
00:14:22,061 --> 00:14:24,796
(Smiling for the first time in a while)

364
00:14:26,239 --> 00:14:28,173
What do you think of her current position?

365
00:14:28,775 --> 00:14:30,309
Her position is slightly in right now.

366
00:14:30,636 --> 00:14:35,106
The opponents up front are
slightly forward in defense.

367
00:14:35,449 --> 00:14:37,682
When they play forward like this,

368
00:14:37,817 --> 00:14:40,152
it's fine to hit the ball
aiming at their faces.

369
00:14:40,887 --> 00:14:43,288
If you hit it like this,
how could they dare move in?

370
00:14:43,890 --> 00:14:45,057
Do you get it?

371
00:14:45,158 --> 00:14:46,492
Just go for a cross-court hit.

372
00:14:47,026 --> 00:14:47,959
Listen.

373
00:14:47,960 --> 00:14:53,364
(She's been emphasizing attacks
down the line.)

374
00:14:53,800 --> 00:14:56,735
A few of you like
hitting cross-court hits.

375
00:14:57,069 --> 00:14:59,204
Just hit it like that
as much as you want today.

376
00:15:00,006 --> 00:15:00,839
Do you get it?

377
00:15:00,840 --> 00:15:03,241
(The master of cross-court attacks is
unleashed.)

378
00:15:04,577 --> 00:15:07,312
(They're playing forward defense,
just as Yeon Koung said.)

379
00:15:08,114 --> 00:15:10,749
(And a cross-court attack executed)

380
00:15:11,367 --> 00:15:12,183
(It worked!)

381
00:15:12,184 --> 00:15:13,317
She's happy.

382
00:15:13,319 --> 00:15:14,853
Enkhsoyol turns out to smile a lot.

383
00:15:14,954 --> 00:15:17,355
The score is 8 to 3, a 5-point difference.

384
00:15:18,257 --> 00:15:20,825
(Careful despite the five-point lead)

385
00:15:21,327 --> 00:15:22,861
Yes, got it!

386
00:15:23,096 --> 00:15:24,162
The receive was a bit too short.

387
00:15:24,297 --> 00:15:25,464
Hit it!

388
00:15:25,865 --> 00:15:26,698
Spike.

389
00:15:28,501 --> 00:15:29,534
- She kept the ball alive!
- She saved it.

390
00:15:29,669 --> 00:15:30,669
Get ready. Nice job!

391
00:15:32,471 --> 00:15:33,539
Is she sending the ball?

392
00:15:33,873 --> 00:15:34,739
Send it!

393
00:15:35,675 --> 00:15:36,708
It's too long!

394
00:15:36,709 --> 00:15:40,412
(It's too long?)

395
00:15:40,813 --> 00:15:42,046
Nice toss.

396
00:15:43,216 --> 00:15:44,316
Let's go, Enkhsoyol!

397
00:15:44,650 --> 00:15:46,217
Hit it!

398
00:15:46,452 --> 00:15:48,420
- In 1, 2.
- Number three!

399
00:15:48,421 --> 00:15:49,688
Hey!

400
00:15:50,022 --> 00:15:53,092
(She targeted the player coming up front.)

401
00:15:53,093 --> 00:15:54,737
Let's go!

402
00:15:55,442 --> 00:15:56,903
(Smash!)

403
00:16:01,275 --> 00:16:04,010
- There she goes, Enkhsoyol.
- Nice.

404
00:16:04,011 --> 00:16:05,979
- The defense was nice.
- Good job.

405
00:16:06,547 --> 00:16:07,914
That's right!

406
00:16:08,049 --> 00:16:08,948
Awesome!

407
00:16:09,517 --> 00:16:11,485
Great job, Enkhsoyol!

408
00:16:11,485 --> 00:16:12,719
(Enkhsoyol's spike ruled the court.)

409
00:16:14,155 --> 00:16:17,591
(Frozen)

410
00:16:19,835 --> 00:16:21,625
(Sigh)

411
00:16:22,644 --> 00:16:23,944
(Getting up quietly)

412
00:16:23,945 --> 00:16:25,946
(Clapping)

413
00:16:25,947 --> 00:16:27,181
Enkhsoyol.

414
00:16:29,044 --> 00:16:30,411
(High-five)

415
00:16:31,447 --> 00:16:33,181
Setter, back to your position!

416
00:16:33,181 --> 00:16:34,148
(Enkhsoyol is awake.)

417
00:16:35,317 --> 00:16:39,687
(The Mongolian girl, Strong Enkhsoyol!)

418
00:16:40,155 --> 00:16:41,956
(The game continues.)

419
00:16:43,325 --> 00:16:44,926
(The cross-court attack is blocked
this time.)

420
00:16:46,463 --> 00:16:48,431
- A free ball.
- They'll move on to the next play.

421
00:16:48,997 --> 00:16:49,863
Watch the player!

422
00:16:50,159 --> 00:16:51,226
Watch Enkhsoyol's movement!

423
00:16:52,901 --> 00:16:53,868
Spike!

424
00:16:54,436 --> 00:16:56,437
Enkhsoyol scores down the line!

425
00:16:58,207 --> 00:16:59,974
- She's on another level.
- Blocking can't block her.

426
00:17:00,689 --> 00:17:03,658
(Taking advantage of opponents
who've gotten used to cross-court hits)

427
00:17:04,171 --> 00:17:05,872
That was too fast.

428
00:17:05,873 --> 00:17:07,560
(Smart Enkhsoyol!)

429
00:17:08,558 --> 00:17:12,594
(Look at you! I didn't even have
to tell you what to do.)

430
00:17:13,855 --> 00:17:16,924
- That's what she's capable of!
- Indeed.

431
00:17:17,984 --> 00:17:18,836
(Kwangju Women's University 3
: Wonder Dogs 7)

432
00:17:18,837 --> 00:17:20,828
(Kwangju Women's University 3
: Wonder Dogs 8)

433
00:17:20,829 --> 00:17:22,997
(Kwangju Women's University 3
: Wonder Dogs 9)

434
00:17:22,998 --> 00:17:24,565
(Kwangju Women's University 3
: Wonder Dogs 10)

435
00:17:25,380 --> 00:17:27,468
(Enkhsoyol is showing explosive potential,
with a run of three.)

436
00:17:27,469 --> 00:17:28,302
Jump!

437
00:17:28,303 --> 00:17:30,237
(Getting a headache)

438
00:17:30,939 --> 00:17:32,906
(A deep sigh)

439
00:17:33,842 --> 00:17:35,709
Do your best until the end!

440
00:17:36,445 --> 00:17:38,012
Go get it!

441
00:17:38,013 --> 00:17:39,647
This time, the set goes to the left.

442
00:17:39,648 --> 00:17:40,615
Smash it.

443
00:17:42,050 --> 00:17:44,518
- Enkhsoyol scores!
- That's good.

444
00:17:45,287 --> 00:17:47,221
- Nice.
- Nice job.

445
00:17:51,793 --> 00:17:53,360
Well received, and back toss.

446
00:17:56,064 --> 00:17:57,364
Dink!

447
00:18:00,102 --> 00:18:01,169
Good job, Enkhsoyol.

448
00:18:03,605 --> 00:18:06,640
(Second set, Kwangju Women's University 5
: Wonder Dogs 18)

449
00:18:10,652 --> 00:18:14,419
(He's no longer energetic
compared to the start of the second set.)

450
00:18:17,845 --> 00:18:19,011
(Scratching his head)

451
00:18:19,245 --> 00:18:22,145
Coach Choi has gone quiet.

452
00:18:25,678 --> 00:18:27,145
The score gap is huge.

453
00:18:28,311 --> 00:18:32,511
(She's happy as the team begins
to attack more successfully.)

454
00:18:32,511 --> 00:18:35,011
This is the score we've waited...

455
00:18:35,011 --> 00:18:36,545
- and missed.
- You're right.

456
00:18:36,945 --> 00:18:38,011
Sub.

457
00:18:39,745 --> 00:18:43,445
Coach Kim makes substitutions
for some of her players.

458
00:18:44,711 --> 00:18:46,178
(Glancing)

459
00:18:46,178 --> 00:18:49,511
She must think
that her team has to keep the lead.

460
00:18:49,778 --> 00:18:53,578
(Second set, Kwangju Women's University 5
: Wonder Dogs 18)

461
00:18:54,178 --> 00:18:57,078
(Lee Jin serves.)

462
00:19:01,445 --> 00:19:02,811
Her serve is so strong.

463
00:19:04,878 --> 00:19:06,478
(A free ball right away)

464
00:19:06,478 --> 00:19:07,478
Mine!

465
00:19:07,478 --> 00:19:08,578
That's it.

466
00:19:09,311 --> 00:19:10,745
Lee Jin.

467
00:19:13,078 --> 00:19:14,845
Spike to the right!

468
00:19:14,845 --> 00:19:15,845
They score!

469
00:19:17,111 --> 00:19:18,911
(Substitutions work perfectly.)

470
00:19:18,911 --> 00:19:20,678
Way to go, Young In!

471
00:19:22,011 --> 00:19:23,645
Koo Sol saves the ball.

472
00:19:23,645 --> 00:19:24,845
It's tossed to Tamira.

473
00:19:24,845 --> 00:19:25,911
Yoon Young In.

474
00:19:26,978 --> 00:19:28,245
(A quick dig)

475
00:19:29,678 --> 00:19:30,878
(Tamira's relentless defense)

476
00:19:30,878 --> 00:19:32,145
Tamira blocked in no time.

477
00:19:32,678 --> 00:19:34,711
(Will it be a touchout?)

478
00:19:36,278 --> 00:19:38,078
(She saved it!)

479
00:19:38,678 --> 00:19:39,811
The ball goes over.

480
00:19:40,178 --> 00:19:41,411
A free ball!

481
00:19:41,411 --> 00:19:42,545
They must seize their chance.

482
00:19:42,545 --> 00:19:43,545
Starting with Enkhsoyol.

483
00:19:43,545 --> 00:19:44,711
In 1, 2!

484
00:19:44,711 --> 00:19:46,011
Spike to the right!

485
00:19:46,011 --> 00:19:47,978
(They saved the ball again!)

486
00:19:48,745 --> 00:19:50,078
Spike but it's touched!

487
00:19:50,078 --> 00:19:52,678
(Teams constantly change
between attacks and defenses.)

488
00:19:53,145 --> 00:19:54,678
You need to hit it!

489
00:19:55,611 --> 00:19:56,611
It goes to the middle.

490
00:19:56,611 --> 00:19:57,645
(A tip to an empty spot)

491
00:19:58,111 --> 00:19:59,911
- Is it saved?
- They defended it.

492
00:19:59,911 --> 00:20:02,178
(Defending is over. Time to attack.)

493
00:20:04,078 --> 00:20:06,478
The Wonder Dogs make a counterattack!

494
00:20:06,478 --> 00:20:09,478
Tamira scores with a touchout!

495
00:20:09,478 --> 00:20:13,145
(Second set, Kwangju Women's University 9
: Wonder Dogs 23)

496
00:20:13,278 --> 00:20:16,245
Substituted players are doing
really great right now.

497
00:20:16,245 --> 00:20:17,411
Exactly.

498
00:20:17,411 --> 00:20:19,611
(Substituted players continue to rise.)

499
00:20:20,011 --> 00:20:21,045
- Yoon Young In.
- Nice.

500
00:20:21,045 --> 00:20:22,545
They score with a block out.

501
00:20:22,845 --> 00:20:25,211
(It's also thanks to Sol's great toss.)

502
00:20:25,511 --> 00:20:27,045
Let's keep going.

503
00:20:27,778 --> 00:20:29,778
It's Wonder Dogs' second set point.

504
00:20:30,545 --> 00:20:31,678
Yoon Young In.

505
00:20:32,345 --> 00:20:33,978
She did it!

506
00:20:33,978 --> 00:20:35,678
It's 25 to 9.

507
00:20:35,678 --> 00:20:39,145
The Wonder Dogs win the second set
with their perfect play.

508
00:20:39,545 --> 00:20:44,078
(It's a shutout victory
when they win one more set.)

509
00:20:44,478 --> 00:20:47,845
You didn't train
just to get nine points, did you?

510
00:20:49,611 --> 00:20:52,478
(Kwangju Women's University is gloomy
after losing twice.)

511
00:20:52,645 --> 00:20:54,178
Hit it with confidence!

512
00:20:56,311 --> 00:20:57,545
Don't you have those guts?

513
00:20:57,545 --> 00:20:58,545
We do.

514
00:20:58,545 --> 00:21:01,878
I would have hit the wall angrily
if I were you.

515
00:21:04,545 --> 00:21:07,011
(Sighing)

516
00:21:07,511 --> 00:21:09,345
Give everything you've got here.

517
00:21:09,345 --> 00:21:10,345
- Got it?
- Yes.

518
00:21:10,345 --> 00:21:12,345
- Do your best in the third set.
- Yes, Coach.

519
00:21:13,078 --> 00:21:14,511
- Let's do this.
- Yes.

520
00:21:14,511 --> 00:21:15,678
Kwangju!

521
00:21:16,145 --> 00:21:17,178
Let's go!

522
00:21:17,178 --> 00:21:18,445
(Let's give our all.)

523
00:21:18,611 --> 00:21:21,045
This is our last chance. A do-or-die.

524
00:21:21,945 --> 00:21:23,311
In 1, 2, 3.

525
00:21:23,311 --> 00:21:25,745
- Think while you play.
- Okay.

526
00:21:25,745 --> 00:21:28,945
The Wonder Dogs shouldn't think
of the gap now...

527
00:21:28,945 --> 00:21:30,578
- but keep pushing forward.
- That's right.

528
00:21:30,578 --> 00:21:32,978
They need a shutout victory
in today's match.

529
00:21:33,745 --> 00:21:36,011
The team must stay focused until the end.

530
00:21:37,145 --> 00:21:38,711
(Third set, Kwangju Women's University 0
: Wonder Dogs 0)

531
00:21:38,721 --> 00:21:40,067
- The third set starts.
- Serve!

532
00:21:47,278 --> 00:21:48,311
(Nice block.)

533
00:21:48,311 --> 00:21:49,745
They blocked it well.

534
00:21:54,645 --> 00:21:58,478
- She hit the ball straight.
- I'm sorry.

535
00:21:58,778 --> 00:22:01,411
Song Hee, the ball was here.
Why did you jump left?

536
00:22:01,411 --> 00:22:02,578
I tried to use my right hand.

537
00:22:02,578 --> 00:22:04,378
- Why your right hand?
- It's my mistake.

538
00:22:04,711 --> 00:22:06,311
(Satisfied)

539
00:22:07,145 --> 00:22:09,045
(Glaring)

540
00:22:09,678 --> 00:22:11,111
Enkhsoyol, how should you hit?

541
00:22:11,711 --> 00:22:12,845
Deeply.

542
00:22:12,845 --> 00:22:14,445
- Hit it deep.
- Yes.

543
00:22:14,911 --> 00:22:16,911
(Go deeper.)

544
00:22:22,178 --> 00:22:23,211
A back toss.

545
00:22:23,211 --> 00:22:24,445
(The ball is in the air.)

546
00:22:24,878 --> 00:22:26,845
(Remember. Go deeper!)

547
00:22:31,211 --> 00:22:32,411
She launches a cross-court spike!

548
00:22:32,411 --> 00:22:34,345
(A successful deep attack)

549
00:22:34,345 --> 00:22:35,711
Serve.

550
00:22:35,711 --> 00:22:37,878
(Third set, Kwangju Women's University 1
: Wonder Dogs 1)

551
00:22:38,611 --> 00:22:40,545
(Smiling)

552
00:22:42,045 --> 00:22:43,045
Min Chae.

553
00:22:43,345 --> 00:22:45,278
I'll handle this.

554
00:22:45,278 --> 00:22:47,011
- Just do it boldly, okay?
- Yes, Coach!

555
00:22:47,599 --> 00:22:48,783
Just throw it in the middle.

556
00:22:53,111 --> 00:22:54,178
Enkhsoyol serves.

557
00:22:56,011 --> 00:22:57,645
Okay. Move!

558
00:22:57,645 --> 00:22:59,478
Tip it! Set it up!

559
00:23:00,411 --> 00:23:01,445
To the left.

560
00:23:02,411 --> 00:23:03,411
Tip!
Koo Hye In!

561
00:23:05,411 --> 00:23:06,445
Sorry!

562
00:23:06,945 --> 00:23:08,145
(Out in the end)

563
00:23:08,145 --> 00:23:09,578
It's a block touchout.

564
00:23:09,578 --> 00:23:12,378
(Yay!)

565
00:23:13,645 --> 00:23:15,911
Coach Choi's instruction worked perfectly.

566
00:23:17,211 --> 00:23:19,711
It's a score from Kim Min Chae,
who was a pro player.

567
00:23:20,111 --> 00:23:21,145
Let's go!

568
00:23:27,545 --> 00:23:28,878
Setting high with an underhand.

569
00:23:30,078 --> 00:23:31,078
It goes over the net.

570
00:23:31,078 --> 00:23:32,178
(The ball goes
to Kwangju Women's University.)

571
00:23:32,178 --> 00:23:33,611
Deep and straight!

572
00:23:34,745 --> 00:23:36,311
(Tossing deeply)

573
00:23:38,311 --> 00:23:39,378
Spike!

574
00:23:39,378 --> 00:23:41,345
(A touchout)

575
00:23:41,345 --> 00:23:43,311
Touch!

576
00:23:45,445 --> 00:23:48,278
Kwangju Women's University is
using deep attacks.

577
00:23:48,511 --> 00:23:50,878
Block it properly!

578
00:23:51,378 --> 00:23:54,045
It's one to three,
so they should start focusing now.

579
00:23:54,045 --> 00:23:55,145
Don't forget...

580
00:23:55,145 --> 00:23:57,745
- the last international match.
- That's right.

581
00:23:58,645 --> 00:24:01,711
(Even though they won two sets,
they shouldn't let their guard down.)

582
00:24:02,311 --> 00:24:04,478
(They can lose their momentum any time.)

583
00:24:05,378 --> 00:24:06,511
(When everyone is nervous...)

584
00:24:06,511 --> 00:24:08,678
Song Hee, I should be here.

585
00:24:08,678 --> 00:24:09,678
Go there.

586
00:24:10,678 --> 00:24:12,878
(Song Hee has a specific spot
for the reception.)

587
00:24:13,145 --> 00:24:15,278
(But she's not sure where to stay.)

588
00:24:17,178 --> 00:24:18,711
Is this her first time in?

589
00:24:21,045 --> 00:24:23,778
(Also, during the second set,)

590
00:24:24,245 --> 00:24:26,278
Tamira, get out of there!

591
00:24:26,278 --> 00:24:27,278
What are you doing?

592
00:24:27,578 --> 00:24:29,645
(Tamira was in the wrong spot.)

593
00:24:30,245 --> 00:24:31,445
I'll mark number 2.

594
00:24:32,245 --> 00:24:34,378
Enkhsoyol, I told you to receive!

595
00:24:34,811 --> 00:24:36,278
What's wrong with you?

596
00:24:36,678 --> 00:24:37,745
This should be easy.

597
00:24:37,745 --> 00:24:39,478
Do I have to tell you this?

598
00:24:40,145 --> 00:24:42,945
It's a basic!

599
00:24:44,145 --> 00:24:47,978
(She's frustrated as players keep
standing in the wrong positions.)

600
00:24:48,378 --> 00:24:50,711
(Kim Na Hyeon serves.)

601
00:24:53,445 --> 00:24:54,811
Pyo Seung Ju receives the ball.

602
00:24:54,811 --> 00:24:55,878
A back toss.

603
00:25:04,078 --> 00:25:06,811
(The Wonder Dogs get a point.)

604
00:25:07,278 --> 00:25:08,911
- What are you doing?
- I'm sorry!

605
00:25:09,678 --> 00:25:12,178
Hey, why didn't you say "Mine?"

606
00:25:12,578 --> 00:25:13,645
You want to get out?

607
00:25:13,645 --> 00:25:14,878
- No!
- No, Coach!

608
00:25:16,845 --> 00:25:18,178
Is this your first time on the court?

609
00:25:18,445 --> 00:25:19,811
- No, Coach.
- How can you not know your spot?

610
00:25:19,811 --> 00:25:20,811
I'm sorry.

611
00:25:21,645 --> 00:25:23,963
Min Chae and Eun Jin,
exchange signs fast to work together!

612
00:25:23,964 --> 00:25:24,811
(Their goal is a comeback win.)
(Their goal is a shutout.)

613
00:25:25,678 --> 00:25:27,145
This is frustrating.

614
00:25:27,511 --> 00:25:30,245
(Two rookie coaches' battle of pride...)

615
00:25:30,245 --> 00:25:32,278
(intensifies.)

616
00:25:32,278 --> 00:25:34,111
(Third set, Kwangju Women's University 4
: Wonder Dogs 4)

617
00:25:34,745 --> 00:25:36,811
(The game continues.)

618
00:25:38,945 --> 00:25:41,411
- She scores, and the tables turn!
- That was a nice play.

619
00:25:41,978 --> 00:25:43,511
(That's it!)

620
00:25:43,978 --> 00:25:46,111
(When the Wonder Dogs score,)

621
00:25:46,711 --> 00:25:48,911
(he checks on them immediately.)

622
00:25:51,811 --> 00:25:53,545
All right. Slow down!

623
00:25:53,545 --> 00:25:55,078
Mark where you'll hit, run, and smash it!

624
00:25:55,445 --> 00:25:56,711
(Run...)

625
00:25:56,711 --> 00:25:58,211
(and smash!)

626
00:26:01,211 --> 00:26:02,211
Hey!

627
00:26:03,011 --> 00:26:05,178
(With Coach Choi's instructions,
Kwangju Women's University catches up.)

628
00:26:06,145 --> 00:26:08,178
(Third set, Kwangju Women's University 7
: Wonder Dogs 9)

629
00:26:09,278 --> 00:26:12,245
Sol!

630
00:26:13,745 --> 00:26:15,745
Setter Koo Sol goes in.

631
00:26:15,745 --> 00:26:18,011
Lee Jin is out, and Koo Sol is in.

632
00:26:20,245 --> 00:26:22,311
Set it from above, Sol.

633
00:26:22,311 --> 00:26:23,445
- Yes, Coach.
- Make sure it's speedy.

634
00:26:24,245 --> 00:26:27,445
Koo Sol has been doing well recently.

635
00:26:27,445 --> 00:26:28,445
Great.

636
00:26:28,611 --> 00:26:30,978
(Son Eun Jin serves.)

637
00:26:30,978 --> 00:26:32,911
It's a short serve!

638
00:26:34,645 --> 00:26:36,345
Son Eun Jin serves.

639
00:26:37,745 --> 00:26:38,845
Enkhsoyol receives.

640
00:26:39,445 --> 00:26:41,178
(Glancing)

641
00:26:42,245 --> 00:26:44,345
(Quickly tossing to Enkhsoyol)

642
00:26:44,878 --> 00:26:47,945
(Defending inside)

643
00:26:48,511 --> 00:26:51,678
(How dare you move in,
in front of strong Enkhsoyol?)

644
00:26:52,111 --> 00:26:54,411
(Remember the cross-court spike?)

645
00:26:55,178 --> 00:26:57,011
(Okay. Got it!)

646
00:27:00,211 --> 00:27:01,511
They get a point with a blockout!

647
00:27:01,516 --> 00:27:03,111
(Enkhsoyol scores with a blockout.)

648
00:27:03,478 --> 00:27:05,411
(Nice toss.)

649
00:27:05,411 --> 00:27:07,345
(And nice attack.)

650
00:27:10,678 --> 00:27:11,811
- Nice one, Sol.
- Yes, Coach.

651
00:27:13,111 --> 00:27:16,378
(Third set, Kwangju Women's University 7
: Wonder Dogs 12)

652
00:27:18,378 --> 00:27:19,711
They saved the ball.

653
00:27:20,445 --> 00:27:21,678
- A push shot to the middle!
- That's great.

654
00:27:21,678 --> 00:27:22,678
They did it!

655
00:27:23,778 --> 00:27:26,978
(Third set, Kwangju Women's University 8
: Wonder Dogs 15)

656
00:27:26,978 --> 00:27:29,445
Enkhsoyol, that was a nice push.

657
00:27:30,345 --> 00:27:32,011
Coach Kim's expression seems to...

658
00:27:32,011 --> 00:27:34,545
- Soften a little.
- Right.

659
00:27:35,545 --> 00:27:37,445
(The game continues.)

660
00:27:37,445 --> 00:27:38,511
Koo Sol.

661
00:27:41,978 --> 00:27:44,883
- Enkhsoyol spikes deep inside the court!
- Well done!

662
00:27:44,884 --> 00:27:46,345
(Scoring in a row
thanks to tosses for Enkhsoyol)

663
00:27:47,945 --> 00:27:50,078
(The Wonder Dogs seize their clear lead.)

664
00:27:50,078 --> 00:27:51,178
It's 17 to 9.

665
00:27:53,311 --> 00:27:54,811
Next is Enkhsoyol's serve.

666
00:27:56,011 --> 00:27:57,345
Go deeply.

667
00:27:58,345 --> 00:27:59,445
Yes!

668
00:28:00,745 --> 00:28:01,778
Serve!

669
00:28:05,078 --> 00:28:06,145
Oh, dear.

670
00:28:06,911 --> 00:28:09,445
(Still improving)

671
00:28:09,855 --> 00:28:11,622
- What did I tell you when you served?
- Make it long.

672
00:28:11,824 --> 00:28:13,659
- If you do, will it graze the net?
- No.

673
00:28:13,659 --> 00:28:14,992
Then make it long!

674
00:28:14,993 --> 00:28:16,660
Yes! That was a mistake!

675
00:28:18,130 --> 00:28:19,030
(After the serve error)
My ball!

676
00:28:20,566 --> 00:28:21,766
- Get it up!
- Sol.

677
00:28:21,767 --> 00:28:22,667
Darn it.

678
00:28:24,503 --> 00:28:25,369
Get it up!

679
00:28:25,804 --> 00:28:26,537
(The setting suddenly becomes unstable.)

680
00:28:26,538 --> 00:28:27,538
They're out of sync.

681
00:28:28,741 --> 00:28:30,241
(Kwangju Women's University's free ball)

682
00:28:30,266 --> 00:28:32,367
Cover it!

683
00:28:34,213 --> 00:28:36,981
(Enkhsoyol fails to defend.)

684
00:28:37,316 --> 00:28:39,418
Enkhsoyol, you should've been
ready already.

685
00:28:39,419 --> 00:28:40,919
Isn't that too obvious?

686
00:28:40,919 --> 00:28:41,752
Okay.

687
00:28:42,697 --> 00:28:45,399
Even a single error like that...

688
00:28:45,424 --> 00:28:47,458
ends up costing more than two points.

689
00:28:47,459 --> 00:28:48,526
That's right.

690
00:28:49,862 --> 00:28:51,129
Brace yourselves harder
at times like this!

691
00:28:51,130 --> 00:28:52,397
(The opponent's error is our chance.)

692
00:28:53,232 --> 00:28:54,165
Hit it!

693
00:28:54,933 --> 00:28:57,601
No, they need to regroup.

694
00:28:58,170 --> 00:28:59,403
What was that?

695
00:29:00,272 --> 00:29:01,572
Take it slow!

696
00:29:01,774 --> 00:29:03,374
Do it again! Hit it!

697
00:29:05,078 --> 00:29:08,546
A play like that can be very dangerous.

698
00:29:08,547 --> 00:29:13,084
The Wonder Dogs keep making errors
while they remain disordered.

699
00:29:13,385 --> 00:29:15,219
Min Chae, don't use too much strength.

700
00:29:15,220 --> 00:29:17,188
- Use your snap!
- Yes, Coach.

701
00:29:18,357 --> 00:29:19,190
That's it! One.

702
00:29:19,892 --> 00:29:20,625
- Go!
- Good!

703
00:29:20,626 --> 00:29:22,327
(Spike using snap)

704
00:29:22,594 --> 00:29:23,527
Good!

705
00:29:24,363 --> 00:29:27,567
The players of Kwangju Women's University
are now...

706
00:29:27,567 --> 00:29:29,400
moving very differently on the court.

707
00:29:30,041 --> 00:29:31,575
Now! Hit it!

708
00:29:31,970 --> 00:29:33,170
Now! Hit it!

709
00:29:33,172 --> 00:29:34,372
Let's go, Min Chae!

710
00:29:34,373 --> 00:29:36,007
That's another point!

711
00:29:36,008 --> 00:29:37,209
(Score by block out)

712
00:29:37,210 --> 00:29:38,042
Nice!

713
00:29:38,510 --> 00:29:40,010
Yes!

714
00:29:40,012 --> 00:29:41,980
(Third set, Kwangju Women's University 16
: Wonder Dogs 21)

715
00:29:41,980 --> 00:29:44,081
Let's get our points up!

716
00:29:44,289 --> 00:29:46,290
Now, the Wonder Dogs can't afford
to lose any more points.

717
00:29:47,586 --> 00:29:49,453
That's it! Hit it!

718
00:29:50,255 --> 00:29:51,989
(The coach is maneuvering
the players with loud shouts.)

719
00:29:51,990 --> 00:29:54,291
She went for a block out.

720
00:29:54,493 --> 00:29:55,626
(Screaming)

721
00:29:55,627 --> 00:29:58,796
Kwangju Women's University is making
a fierce last spurt to catch up.

722
00:29:58,797 --> 00:29:59,797
(Nervous)

723
00:30:00,399 --> 00:30:01,801
(We must widen the gap again.)

724
00:30:01,802 --> 00:30:02,634
My ball!
Pass it to me!

725
00:30:04,036 --> 00:30:05,503
(She sets it without looking.)

726
00:30:05,504 --> 00:30:06,371
Sol.

727
00:30:06,939 --> 00:30:08,373
(The opposing middle blocker
moves quickly to mark her.)

728
00:30:08,373 --> 00:30:09,473
Stick on the right!

729
00:30:09,474 --> 00:30:11,308
- It was blocked.
- Oh, dear.

730
00:30:11,310 --> 00:30:13,711
(Their attack backfires with a block.)

731
00:30:14,379 --> 00:30:15,245
No!

732
00:30:18,217 --> 00:30:19,918
The gap is down to three points!

733
00:30:19,918 --> 00:30:21,385
(Kwangju Women's University 20
: Wonder Dogs 23)

734
00:30:22,187 --> 00:30:24,922
I thought things weren't going...

735
00:30:25,131 --> 00:30:27,132
the way I wanted.

736
00:30:27,392 --> 00:30:30,961
Since we had already lost two games,

737
00:30:30,963 --> 00:30:33,832
I trusted my players to start strong
from the beginning,

738
00:30:34,266 --> 00:30:37,335
but there were
so many ridiculous mistakes.

739
00:30:37,503 --> 00:30:39,404
I could see...

740
00:30:39,404 --> 00:30:42,106
they weren't doing what we'd trained for.

741
00:30:42,508 --> 00:30:44,242
As their coach, I was frustrated.

742
00:30:44,810 --> 00:30:48,980
I couldn't help but feel disappointed.

743
00:30:50,516 --> 00:30:51,850
(We need to turn things around now!)

744
00:30:51,850 --> 00:30:52,983
Let's do it again.

745
00:30:52,985 --> 00:30:55,420
Sol, watch out for what's coming your way.

746
00:30:56,021 --> 00:30:59,357
You should've passed it
to Enkhsoyol! This is frustrating.

747
00:30:59,358 --> 00:31:01,125
(She keeps Enkhsoyol in check.)

748
00:31:01,293 --> 00:31:02,159
Let's get Enkhsoyol.

749
00:31:02,561 --> 00:31:05,496
Guys, go slow on blocks.

750
00:31:06,598 --> 00:31:10,200
Even though the Wonder Dogs are leading,
they can't let their guard down.

751
00:31:11,103 --> 00:31:11,969
My ball!
Enkhsoyol.

752
00:31:13,114 --> 00:31:14,414
(Peeking)

753
00:31:14,439 --> 00:31:15,205
She receives it.

754
00:31:16,041 --> 00:31:17,942
(She sets to Enkhsoyol this time.)

755
00:31:19,845 --> 00:31:20,745
She receives it.

756
00:31:20,979 --> 00:31:22,146
Spike!

757
00:31:22,481 --> 00:31:23,548
Enkhsoyol.

758
00:31:23,548 --> 00:31:24,515
(Enkhsoyol scores a point!)

759
00:31:24,683 --> 00:31:27,551
Yes!

760
00:31:27,552 --> 00:31:28,919
Good job!

761
00:31:29,521 --> 00:31:32,022
Now, today's game is...

762
00:31:32,100 --> 00:31:33,700
at Wonder Dogs' match point!

763
00:31:33,725 --> 00:31:34,989
One more!

764
00:31:35,594 --> 00:31:37,461
(Glancing)

765
00:31:38,197 --> 00:31:39,664
Sol, to Young In.

766
00:31:39,865 --> 00:31:40,665
Okay.

767
00:31:41,800 --> 00:31:44,636
(Sol and Young In exchange signals.)

768
00:31:44,637 --> 00:31:46,171
Watch the front carefully!

769
00:31:46,171 --> 00:31:48,405
Tamira, watch the front!

770
00:31:48,407 --> 00:31:49,540
(One more point means a win!)

771
00:31:50,742 --> 00:31:52,309
The score is 24 to 21.

772
00:31:53,912 --> 00:31:54,745
Sol.

773
00:31:54,947 --> 00:31:55,713
Spike!

774
00:31:58,517 --> 00:31:59,917
They succeed in defense.

775
00:32:00,385 --> 00:32:01,218
She sets it up high.

776
00:32:02,321 --> 00:32:04,255
The ball rebounds. Tamira!

777
00:32:04,256 --> 00:32:05,176
Pass it!

778
00:32:05,624 --> 00:32:08,226
Now they have a chance to finish the game!

779
00:32:08,235 --> 00:32:09,802
(She passes to Young In as planned.)

780
00:32:14,072 --> 00:32:16,840
(Their attack hits
the empty spot perfectly.)

781
00:32:17,242 --> 00:32:18,676
It's a success!

782
00:32:19,478 --> 00:32:21,125
(Kwangju Women's University 21
: Wonder Dogs 25)

783
00:32:21,126 --> 00:32:22,681
Well done.

784
00:32:22,682 --> 00:32:23,748
That's it!

785
00:32:23,749 --> 00:32:26,417
(What a bummer.)

786
00:32:27,653 --> 00:32:28,620
Yes!

787
00:32:28,620 --> 00:32:30,921
(Against university champs,
Kwangju Women's University)

788
00:32:30,922 --> 00:32:32,556
It's 25 to 21!

789
00:32:32,724 --> 00:32:34,558
The set score is three to nil!

790
00:32:34,559 --> 00:32:37,094
It's a perfect shutout!

791
00:32:37,095 --> 00:32:39,563
The Wonder Dogs now have two wins!

792
00:32:39,564 --> 00:32:41,799
(Set Score)

793
00:32:42,501 --> 00:32:45,803
(But Coach Kim's face doesn't look
as happy as expected.)

794
00:32:49,908 --> 00:32:53,177
This is no joke. Not at all.

795
00:33:16,868 --> 00:33:17,768
My gosh.

796
00:33:19,578 --> 00:33:23,648
Since we won 3 to 0,

797
00:33:23,942 --> 00:33:27,311
it's only right to celebrate.

798
00:33:28,113 --> 00:33:30,715
But there's something I want to ask you.

799
00:33:30,715 --> 00:33:33,884
What did we promise each other
before the game?

800
00:33:34,820 --> 00:33:37,088
To stay extra focused early in the game.

801
00:33:37,522 --> 00:33:42,025
I'm very disappointed about that today.

802
00:33:43,095 --> 00:33:45,096
We know we're not strong in the beginning,

803
00:33:45,096 --> 00:33:46,396
so we planned to stay focused early.

804
00:33:46,598 --> 00:33:48,899
As the starting lineup,

805
00:33:48,900 --> 00:33:52,169
do you think you fulfilled
your responsibilities today?

806
00:33:55,207 --> 00:33:58,376
Myoung Hwa, why do you think
I put you in the starting lineup?

807
00:34:02,013 --> 00:34:04,149
- You were chosen, right?
- Yes.

808
00:34:04,150 --> 00:34:05,949
Is that all you got when you're chosen?

809
00:34:05,951 --> 00:34:07,351
You were there from the start.

810
00:34:07,352 --> 00:34:08,852
You let them score an easy point.

811
00:34:08,854 --> 00:34:10,388
(Lead lost early due to a defensive error)

812
00:34:10,388 --> 00:34:11,655
You couldn't even find your position.

813
00:34:11,656 --> 00:34:13,624
(She even failed
to locate her reception spot.)

814
00:34:13,625 --> 00:34:16,994
Everyone was so sloppy.

815
00:34:17,696 --> 00:34:19,363
We can't let this happen again.

816
00:34:20,532 --> 00:34:22,733
Remember why you're on this team.

817
00:34:22,734 --> 00:34:23,901
Stop forgetting.

818
00:34:23,902 --> 00:34:25,469
Don't you remember...

819
00:34:25,470 --> 00:34:27,071
how desperate you were during tryouts?

820
00:34:27,406 --> 00:34:28,573
Weren't you desperate?

821
00:34:28,774 --> 00:34:29,607
- We were.
- Yes.

822
00:34:30,342 --> 00:34:32,476
I think you've all forgotten that.

823
00:34:32,477 --> 00:34:35,420
Are you satisfied with where you are now?
You think it's all guaranteed?

824
00:34:36,182 --> 00:34:38,349
What happened? You think it's all set now?

825
00:34:39,351 --> 00:34:40,751
That's how you look to me.

826
00:34:41,586 --> 00:34:43,020
I told the producer earlier...

827
00:34:43,021 --> 00:34:44,655
that we may have to let
some of the players go.

828
00:34:45,123 --> 00:34:46,390
We need to get rid of some of you.

829
00:34:46,658 --> 00:34:48,959
That's because you're not giving your all.

830
00:34:49,094 --> 00:34:52,096
You're so different from
when we first formed this team.

831
00:34:52,364 --> 00:34:53,431
That's how I see it.

832
00:34:55,133 --> 00:34:57,401
And if you look that way, it means
that's exactly what you're doing,

833
00:34:57,402 --> 00:34:58,602
doesn't it?

834
00:34:58,904 --> 00:35:01,772
We can't keep players
who don't give their best...

835
00:35:02,274 --> 00:35:03,674
and fall behind.

836
00:35:03,675 --> 00:35:05,543
That's the only conclusion I've reached.

837
00:35:05,911 --> 00:35:08,546
None of you has shown me
anything new lately.

838
00:35:09,815 --> 00:35:11,849
Displaying your brilliance is...

839
00:35:12,617 --> 00:35:15,185
the only way to get
the corporate teams interested in you.

840
00:35:15,186 --> 00:35:18,655
But I don't think my players
even care about that anymore.

841
00:35:18,657 --> 00:35:20,091
That's why I thought...

842
00:35:20,091 --> 00:35:22,059
maybe we need something impactful,

843
00:35:22,160 --> 00:35:23,861
a wake-up call,

844
00:35:24,296 --> 00:35:26,797
and that's why I brought
up the idea of elimination.

845
00:35:27,032 --> 00:35:29,866
As a coach, it's my job keep
my players alert and sharp.

846
00:35:30,235 --> 00:35:32,870
You need to think this through.

847
00:35:33,238 --> 00:35:36,807
Today's 3-to-0 victory was wonderful.

848
00:35:37,075 --> 00:35:39,343
But performance-wise, I saw that you still
haven't broken your bad habits.

849
00:35:39,344 --> 00:35:41,545
You've forgotten what we trained for.

850
00:35:42,113 --> 00:35:44,514
You need to reset your minds like pros.

851
00:35:44,983 --> 00:35:46,450
It's not about how hard you trained,

852
00:35:46,451 --> 00:35:50,120
it's about how you stay
mentally prepared like professionals.

853
00:35:50,422 --> 00:35:53,157
That's how you play better
and play real volleyball.

854
00:35:54,826 --> 00:35:56,126
Do you understand?

855
00:35:56,330 --> 00:35:57,461
- Yes, coach.
- Yes.

856
00:35:57,729 --> 00:36:00,064
That's what we call
the foundation of volleyball.

857
00:36:00,298 --> 00:36:02,399
It felt like getting hit in the head.

858
00:36:02,601 --> 00:36:05,102
We can't repeat today's performance again.

859
00:36:05,103 --> 00:36:07,738
We should focus a bit harder
on the next match.

860
00:36:07,739 --> 00:36:10,507
And to do that, we must get
it together, starting from practice.

861
00:36:11,309 --> 00:36:13,176
Now, I'll announce our next opponent.

862
00:36:17,249 --> 00:36:19,984
(Wonder Dogs' Current Win Rate)

863
00:36:19,985 --> 00:36:21,385
(Two wins and two losses)

864
00:36:21,386 --> 00:36:22,820
(Win rate: 50 percent)

865
00:36:22,821 --> 00:36:25,556
(Their next opponent is...)

866
00:36:25,557 --> 00:36:28,125
(Suwon Special City)

867
00:36:28,651 --> 00:36:30,051
(Kim Na Hee)

868
00:36:30,435 --> 00:36:32,136
(Back Chae Rim)

869
00:36:32,531 --> 00:36:34,198
(Yoon Young In)

870
00:36:34,733 --> 00:36:37,382
(Volleyball Futures Champion
Danyang Tournament 2025)

871
00:36:37,402 --> 00:36:41,452
(Suwon Special City Volleyball Team)

872
00:36:45,437 --> 00:36:48,837
I'm Kang Min Sik,
coach of the Suwon City Hall team.

873
00:36:48,837 --> 00:36:51,404
I have sent 14 players to the pro team.

874
00:36:51,871 --> 00:36:55,137
(He's produced 14 professional players.)

875
00:36:55,304 --> 00:36:56,904
Three so far this year.

876
00:36:58,910 --> 00:37:02,077
(An underdog specialist,
Coach Kang Min Sik)

877
00:37:02,077 --> 00:37:05,710
Young In is a good player. She is.

878
00:37:05,710 --> 00:37:08,644
But sometimes she hits oddly
or misses out of nowhere.

879
00:37:10,877 --> 00:37:12,977
Na Hee is very fast.

880
00:37:12,977 --> 00:37:15,177
If we're playing against her,
we should rally.

881
00:37:15,177 --> 00:37:16,644
Make her move around a lot.

882
00:37:16,977 --> 00:37:20,610
Because you need to wear down her stamina.

883
00:37:22,010 --> 00:37:23,977
In the case of Chae Rim,

884
00:37:23,977 --> 00:37:25,410
she has a peculiar habit.

885
00:37:25,810 --> 00:37:27,877
If she nods her head,
it means she's losing it.

886
00:37:28,177 --> 00:37:29,410
Her mental game is slipping.

887
00:37:30,177 --> 00:37:32,810
If she's nodding her head,
then she's in trouble.

888
00:37:34,910 --> 00:37:38,710
I see them
and play against them all the time.

889
00:37:38,710 --> 00:37:42,610
They're the ones
whose weaknesses we know best.

890
00:37:43,110 --> 00:37:45,944
Jin's balls are fast,
like they're bouncing off.

891
00:37:45,944 --> 00:37:48,077
Song Hee is short,

892
00:37:48,077 --> 00:37:49,377
but she hits well.

893
00:37:49,377 --> 00:37:50,610
As for Hye In,

894
00:37:50,610 --> 00:37:52,810
she has a wide defensive range,
which is a surprise.

895
00:37:53,444 --> 00:37:54,710
As for Na Yeon...

896
00:37:54,710 --> 00:37:56,410
Enkhsoyol and Tamira...

897
00:37:56,410 --> 00:37:57,944
Hyeon Jeong is...

898
00:37:57,944 --> 00:38:00,477
You know every player on the Wonder Dogs.

899
00:38:00,477 --> 00:38:03,244
Well, you need to know your opponent.

900
00:38:05,444 --> 00:38:07,177
When I enter the gym,

901
00:38:07,177 --> 00:38:09,044
I scan my players from head to toe.

902
00:38:09,544 --> 00:38:12,244
How their facial expressions are
when they're stretching.

903
00:38:12,244 --> 00:38:15,844
If their expression or the way they move
is different from usual,

904
00:38:15,844 --> 00:38:18,010
I call them in for a check.

905
00:38:18,377 --> 00:38:20,210
There's always something that comes up.

906
00:38:21,510 --> 00:38:24,310
You almost sound like a secret agent.

907
00:38:25,344 --> 00:38:27,044
(Sharp)

908
00:38:27,610 --> 00:38:31,410
(What do you think about Coach Yeon Koung,
who has no years of experience?)

909
00:38:31,410 --> 00:38:35,677
When star players become coaches,

910
00:38:35,677 --> 00:38:38,544
they think they can do
what they've been doing on the court...

911
00:38:38,544 --> 00:38:41,444
and expect it to work out at first.

912
00:38:41,444 --> 00:38:44,710
But the game is played by the players,

913
00:38:45,577 --> 00:38:47,044
not the coaches.

914
00:38:49,610 --> 00:38:53,110
This is the first step
for Coach Yeon Koung as a coach,

915
00:38:53,444 --> 00:38:55,310
and she'll need to study a lot for that.

916
00:38:55,310 --> 00:38:56,977
I think...

917
00:38:57,477 --> 00:38:59,710
she'll need a lot of time.

918
00:38:59,710 --> 00:39:02,144
Once you start,
you have to see it through.

919
00:39:02,677 --> 00:39:06,677
(The Wonder Dogs vs. Suwon Special City)

920
00:39:06,677 --> 00:39:08,277
The Suwon team's strength is...

921
00:39:08,277 --> 00:39:12,010
that their players are too good
to pick just one ace.

922
00:39:12,010 --> 00:39:15,610
All their attackers have
strong offensive skills.

923
00:39:15,610 --> 00:39:17,577
When they go up against a good team,

924
00:39:17,577 --> 00:39:19,144
they seem to perform even better.

925
00:39:20,410 --> 00:39:22,544
(How long were you
with Suwon Special City?)

926
00:39:22,544 --> 00:39:24,277
Eight years.

927
00:39:25,310 --> 00:39:26,477
He's like a father to me.

928
00:39:26,477 --> 00:39:27,777
I've known him for way too long.

929
00:39:28,377 --> 00:39:33,177
We're competing against my precious team
with someone subbing for me.

930
00:39:33,710 --> 00:39:36,544
I want them to realize
what it's like without me.

931
00:39:37,877 --> 00:39:40,510
"Chae Rim is making
this game so difficult."

932
00:39:40,510 --> 00:39:42,877
That's what I want them to think
during the game.

933
00:39:42,877 --> 00:39:45,110
We're going to give it our all.

934
00:39:45,110 --> 00:39:46,444
(Playing against their previous team)

935
00:39:46,444 --> 00:39:50,210
I think this might be
the most crucial match.

936
00:39:50,577 --> 00:39:53,677
Because we have two wins and two losses.

937
00:39:54,177 --> 00:39:56,977
If we lose this match,

938
00:39:56,977 --> 00:40:00,010
we might even have to disband.

939
00:40:00,010 --> 00:40:02,944
It could be a crisis situation.

940
00:40:03,244 --> 00:40:04,910
This is a must-win match.

941
00:40:09,877 --> 00:40:12,210
How do you feel about going
against Suwon City Hall?

942
00:40:12,210 --> 00:40:15,944
I want to show what we've learned here.

943
00:40:17,077 --> 00:40:18,410
I think we have to.

944
00:40:18,410 --> 00:40:21,210
I want to too, and I'm excited.

945
00:40:21,210 --> 00:40:24,310
Honestly, I think we have to win
this match...

946
00:40:24,310 --> 00:40:28,010
to show everyone that us joining
the Wonder Dogs and our efforts here...

947
00:40:28,010 --> 00:40:30,610
weren't in vain.

948
00:40:30,877 --> 00:40:35,077
And you guys have a lot more time left
in your careers,

949
00:40:35,077 --> 00:40:38,710
but let's be real.
I don't have that much time left.

950
00:40:38,710 --> 00:40:41,610
That's why each day is precious to me.

951
00:40:41,610 --> 00:40:43,077
And about the match.

952
00:40:47,077 --> 00:40:48,377
What's wrong with me?

953
00:40:50,677 --> 00:40:51,710
I'm fine.

954
00:40:57,410 --> 00:40:58,810
We really respect you.

955
00:40:58,810 --> 00:41:00,910
Well, I don't know.

956
00:41:01,677 --> 00:41:03,877
We just have to do well, no matter what.

957
00:41:03,877 --> 00:41:04,944
We have to.

958
00:41:06,244 --> 00:41:08,677
- We got this, right?
- Yes.

959
00:41:09,777 --> 00:41:11,677
(And the next day)

960
00:41:11,844 --> 00:41:13,644
(Like any other training day)

961
00:41:13,644 --> 00:41:15,410
Closer to the line.

962
00:41:15,410 --> 00:41:17,844
(Under the direction of Coach Yeon Koung,)

963
00:41:19,310 --> 00:41:24,410
(the players finished
an intense training session.)

964
00:41:25,010 --> 00:41:26,044
(The newbie coach is off work.)

965
00:41:26,044 --> 00:41:28,444
Guys, gather around for a warm-up.

966
00:41:28,677 --> 00:41:30,677
Guys, gather around.

967
00:41:30,677 --> 00:41:32,277
(The players are gathering around?)

968
00:41:32,544 --> 00:41:35,577
Are our matches always easy
or hard in the first set?

969
00:41:35,577 --> 00:41:36,477
- It's hard.
- It's hard.

970
00:41:36,477 --> 00:41:38,310
When we practice, do we succeed in...

971
00:41:38,310 --> 00:41:39,677
tipping at our first try?

972
00:41:39,944 --> 00:41:40,910
No, right?

973
00:41:41,677 --> 00:41:45,944
We have to push ourselves harder
in training if we want to win.

974
00:41:45,944 --> 00:41:47,477
We need to get our heads in the game.

975
00:41:47,477 --> 00:41:50,477
We only have one shot left, really.

976
00:41:50,477 --> 00:41:51,610
Everyone, listen up.

977
00:41:51,610 --> 00:41:54,977
Suwon City Hall is
training hard today too...

978
00:41:54,977 --> 00:41:56,010
to beat us.

979
00:41:56,977 --> 00:42:00,010
If we want to win too, we have to work
harder than they do, don't we?

980
00:42:00,277 --> 00:42:01,877
We can't win by just doing
what we always do.

981
00:42:02,577 --> 00:42:04,410
I know we might do well
when we're practicing,

982
00:42:04,410 --> 00:42:05,710
but do we do as well in an actual game?

983
00:42:05,710 --> 00:42:06,810
Not even half of our skills show.

984
00:42:06,810 --> 00:42:09,044
These are the basics.

985
00:42:09,744 --> 00:42:13,777
Coach shouldn't even be ordering
those things during a game.

986
00:42:13,777 --> 00:42:17,277
That's something we all should be
doing on our own.

987
00:42:17,277 --> 00:42:19,744
I think we need to do
some serious self-reflection.

988
00:42:21,044 --> 00:42:22,110
We work so hard in practice,

989
00:42:22,110 --> 00:42:23,544
but we always fail to show that in a game.

990
00:42:23,544 --> 00:42:25,244
(Vice-captain Na Hee leading by example)

991
00:42:25,377 --> 00:42:27,177
We came here to win, didn't we?

992
00:42:28,110 --> 00:42:30,310
Let's give it our all, please.

993
00:42:30,310 --> 00:42:33,377
We need to buckle down
and practice harder.

994
00:42:33,377 --> 00:42:36,544
Everyone practices so desperately.

995
00:42:36,544 --> 00:42:38,210
It's time to show the results.

996
00:42:38,977 --> 00:42:41,010
We need to stick together.

997
00:42:42,177 --> 00:42:44,044
(The next day)

998
00:42:44,444 --> 00:42:45,410
Let's give it our best shot.

999
00:42:45,710 --> 00:42:46,877
- Got it?
- Yes, Coach.

1000
00:42:46,877 --> 00:42:47,977
Nice job, everyone.

1001
00:42:47,977 --> 00:42:50,577
(The video meeting is finished.)

1002
00:42:51,544 --> 00:42:54,410
(Scooting over)

1003
00:42:55,444 --> 00:43:00,210
(Players take pictures of the analysis
with their phones.)

1004
00:43:01,177 --> 00:43:06,810
(Reviewing what they learned
during the day in the dormitory at night)

1005
00:43:06,810 --> 00:43:11,077
Get ready to serve low
and with strong power.

1006
00:43:11,610 --> 00:43:15,077
(Even after that, the two liberos...)

1007
00:43:15,710 --> 00:43:21,610
(kept analyzing the opposing players.)

1008
00:43:21,610 --> 00:43:24,244
(The next meeting day)

1009
00:43:24,710 --> 00:43:27,877
What do you think about Hyo Rim's serve?

1010
00:43:30,644 --> 00:43:33,010
It's shaky, but it's not fast,

1011
00:43:33,010 --> 00:43:34,744
so we should keep moving and pass it.

1012
00:43:36,744 --> 00:43:37,544
That's right.

1013
00:43:37,544 --> 00:43:39,410
Here's Yuni. What about Yuni?

1014
00:43:39,810 --> 00:43:42,077
The server is far away, and it's shaky.

1015
00:43:42,077 --> 00:43:45,744
Her serve comes from deep,
with a heavy float.

1016
00:43:46,577 --> 00:43:49,977
(Speaking so smoothly)

1017
00:43:51,510 --> 00:43:52,477
You know it well.

1018
00:43:54,377 --> 00:43:55,410
She already knows everything.

1019
00:43:57,610 --> 00:43:59,710
You know your opponent too well.

1020
00:43:59,977 --> 00:44:01,677
We might just get
a 70 percent receive rate.

1021
00:44:01,677 --> 00:44:02,877
The game of your life.

1022
00:44:05,277 --> 00:44:06,177
Water.

1023
00:44:06,177 --> 00:44:08,510
(This wasn't the only thing that changed.)

1024
00:44:08,944 --> 00:44:11,544
(Another training day)

1025
00:44:12,077 --> 00:44:14,110
(They're taking a short break.)

1026
00:44:15,877 --> 00:44:17,310
(Running)

1027
00:44:17,310 --> 00:44:20,510
Wu Seong, I need your help.
Go there and help me, please.

1028
00:44:21,377 --> 00:44:25,510
(Personal tutoring time during the break)

1029
00:44:26,077 --> 00:44:28,244
(No time to rest)

1030
00:44:28,544 --> 00:44:31,777
(Additional training)

1031
00:44:32,377 --> 00:44:34,977
(Another training session)

1032
00:44:35,610 --> 00:44:36,510
(Staying fully focused)

1033
00:44:36,510 --> 00:44:37,977
Right on! Good job!

1034
00:44:38,444 --> 00:44:39,944
Nice, Hye In. Nice job!

1035
00:44:41,172 --> 00:44:44,572
(Now that the players are in beast mode,)

1036
00:44:45,338 --> 00:44:48,505
(the previous one-sided video meetings...)

1037
00:44:50,605 --> 00:44:55,172
(are now turning
into interactive meeting times.)

1038
00:44:55,338 --> 00:44:56,205
Enkhsoyol.

1039
00:44:56,205 --> 00:44:57,672
(Sending a signal)

1040
00:44:57,805 --> 00:44:59,905
(Just like they discussed
during the video meeting,)

1041
00:45:00,172 --> 00:45:03,138
(they're syncing up
and beginning the training.)

1042
00:45:03,138 --> 00:45:03,938
High ball.

1043
00:45:03,938 --> 00:45:06,172
Enkhsoyol!

1044
00:45:07,605 --> 00:45:11,338
(Successful attack on the gap!)

1045
00:45:12,572 --> 00:45:13,472
Yes!

1046
00:45:15,272 --> 00:45:16,605
(Sticking to what they discussed...)

1047
00:45:16,605 --> 00:45:18,238
(and playing accordingly)

1048
00:45:18,238 --> 00:45:19,472
Nice!

1049
00:45:19,472 --> 00:45:20,805
Nice toss, Sol.

1050
00:45:22,038 --> 00:45:23,772
Low?

1051
00:45:23,772 --> 00:45:25,438
(Okay, got it.)

1052
00:45:26,738 --> 00:45:28,238
(They're communicating...)

1053
00:45:28,238 --> 00:45:30,438
(and driving up their attack efficiency.)

1054
00:45:30,438 --> 00:45:32,972
Tamira, good! Nice job!

1055
00:45:33,772 --> 00:45:34,938
Give us a sign.

1056
00:45:39,005 --> 00:45:40,972
(Flawless teamwork on quick plays!)

1057
00:45:41,859 --> 00:45:43,326
Sol is in good form.

1058
00:45:44,008 --> 00:45:44,775
Get it!

1059
00:45:44,776 --> 00:45:45,809
In 1, 2!

1060
00:45:48,880 --> 00:45:50,214
Enkhsoyol, hit it!

1061
00:45:50,248 --> 00:45:52,015
- Enkhsoyol, get ready for a quick attack.
- Okay.

1062
00:45:52,117 --> 00:45:54,985
Again!

1063
00:45:55,053 --> 00:45:56,087
Step in!

1064
00:45:56,454 --> 00:45:57,688
(With Sol, who is on a roll,)

1065
00:45:57,689 --> 00:45:59,856
- Was it okay?
- Perfect.

1066
00:46:00,725 --> 00:46:03,493
(their teamwork is on fire.)

1067
00:46:07,027 --> 00:46:09,795
(More confident than ever...)

1068
00:46:11,231 --> 00:46:13,866
(with full-power attacks)

1069
00:46:13,867 --> 00:46:15,267
Nice job.

1070
00:46:16,169 --> 00:46:18,303
They've improved a lot.

1071
00:46:19,673 --> 00:46:21,540
What's going? You're scaring me.

1072
00:46:22,476 --> 00:46:24,811
They usually have ups and downs,

1073
00:46:25,312 --> 00:46:27,079
but they're so good that I'm anxious.

1074
00:46:27,080 --> 00:46:28,881
(Laughing)

1075
00:46:29,182 --> 00:46:30,115
I'm anxious.

1076
00:46:32,753 --> 00:46:33,753
What?

1077
00:46:33,954 --> 00:46:34,921
How is her attack so precise?

1078
00:46:35,422 --> 00:46:37,556
They're suddenly playing really well.

1079
00:46:38,267 --> 00:46:42,261
Whether this is real improvement
or just a good day,

1080
00:46:42,396 --> 00:46:43,796
we'll find out tomorrow.

1081
00:46:50,637 --> 00:46:53,572
(Match day)

1082
00:46:54,241 --> 00:46:56,642
I'll do the best I can until the end.

1083
00:46:56,977 --> 00:47:00,313
(They can now even aim
for a win rate above 50 percent.)

1084
00:47:01,948 --> 00:47:03,115
Are you guys all ready?

1085
00:47:03,917 --> 00:47:05,117
- Yes.
- Are you?

1086
00:47:05,519 --> 00:47:08,121
Let's make it happen.
Look at that poor emblem.

1087
00:47:08,822 --> 00:47:10,389
It shrank a lot.

1088
00:47:10,590 --> 00:47:14,026
Let's show what we've got today
so that it won't shrink anymore.

1089
00:47:14,302 --> 00:47:16,436
I'll announce today's starting members.

1090
00:47:18,131 --> 00:47:19,465
Seung Ju, Enkhsoyol,

1091
00:47:19,466 --> 00:47:20,599
Na Hee, Myoung Hwa,

1092
00:47:21,935 --> 00:47:24,136
Song Hee, and Hye In.

1093
00:47:24,538 --> 00:47:27,273
(And the setter is...)

1094
00:47:27,574 --> 00:47:29,441
And Sol.

1095
00:47:30,710 --> 00:47:31,510
Let's go.

1096
00:47:31,511 --> 00:47:33,345
(Included in the starting lineup
for the first time)

1097
00:47:33,590 --> 00:47:35,891
(The coaching staff had a meeting
a few days ago.)

1098
00:47:35,916 --> 00:47:38,251
The one who has improved the most is Sol.

1099
00:47:38,251 --> 00:47:39,351
Yes, she's really good.

1100
00:47:40,020 --> 00:47:42,621
I think it would be best for Sol
to be in the starting lineup first.

1101
00:47:43,490 --> 00:47:46,325
Since yesterday, everyone has been
unanimous about putting Sol in.

1102
00:47:46,593 --> 00:47:47,326
Okay?

1103
00:47:48,228 --> 00:47:49,094
Let's do this.

1104
00:47:49,095 --> 00:47:50,862
I've always been preparing.

1105
00:47:51,198 --> 00:47:52,598
Even if I didn't make the starting lineup,

1106
00:47:52,600 --> 00:47:54,467
I always thought
about how I should play in the game.

1107
00:47:54,468 --> 00:47:56,335
I was really happy when I heard
the announcement earlier,

1108
00:47:56,803 --> 00:47:59,838
and I'll show a good performance
on the court.

1109
00:48:00,507 --> 00:48:02,642
- Hello.
- Hi.

1110
00:48:03,143 --> 00:48:04,777
Look at your tie!

1111
00:48:05,812 --> 00:48:07,079
(Wearing the Wonder Dogs' team color)

1112
00:48:07,080 --> 00:48:08,080
It's the same!

1113
00:48:08,081 --> 00:48:10,349
- I bought it on Coupang for 10 dollars.
- For 10 dollars?

1114
00:48:10,350 --> 00:48:11,817
(Pleased)

1115
00:48:12,252 --> 00:48:14,420
Will there be any changes for this game?

1116
00:48:14,789 --> 00:48:17,390
Against Kwangju Women's University,
Enkhsoyol was at the forefront.

1117
00:48:17,390 --> 00:48:18,590
They may be surprised.

1118
00:48:19,860 --> 00:48:22,762
Sol is in the starting lineup today.

1119
00:48:23,063 --> 00:48:24,330
Today's game is against Suwon City Hall,

1120
00:48:24,331 --> 00:48:27,233
and quite a few players in your team were
Suwon City Hall members,

1121
00:48:27,233 --> 00:48:29,968
so they must know each other very well.

1122
00:48:29,970 --> 00:48:34,773
Did you ignore that in the lineup,
or did you take it into account?

1123
00:48:35,375 --> 00:48:36,413
I didn't take it into account.

1124
00:48:36,414 --> 00:48:38,044
So you're focusing
on what your team can execute best.

1125
00:48:38,044 --> 00:48:39,011
Right.

1126
00:48:39,212 --> 00:48:40,679
(Meanwhile)

1127
00:48:41,214 --> 00:48:43,782
(Another coach,
a specialist on the Wonder Dogs)

1128
00:48:43,783 --> 00:48:48,253
What do you expect
the opposing team's starting lineup to be?

1129
00:48:48,254 --> 00:48:51,423
Sol is tall, so Coach Kim will probably...

1130
00:48:51,925 --> 00:48:57,597
put her in the starting lineup
for that reason.

1131
00:48:57,597 --> 00:48:58,831
(Incredible foresight)

1132
00:48:58,832 --> 00:49:00,066
You secretly spied on them, right?

1133
00:49:00,066 --> 00:49:03,368
I heard a rumor that you secretly peeked
at them training through the window.

1134
00:49:03,637 --> 00:49:05,805
(While training a few days ago)

1135
00:49:06,172 --> 00:49:08,407
(In the middle of reception training)

1136
00:49:12,746 --> 00:49:14,747
(A surprise scout)

1137
00:49:15,148 --> 00:49:18,384
(Boldly not hiding who he is)

1138
00:49:19,243 --> 00:49:21,344
(Staring intently)

1139
00:49:22,088 --> 00:49:26,125
(Analyzing the Wonder Dogs' full strength)

1140
00:49:26,126 --> 00:49:27,893
You could've casually walked in.

1141
00:49:27,894 --> 00:49:29,027
I realized one thing there.

1142
00:49:29,029 --> 00:49:30,863
I saw their serve-receive drill,

1143
00:49:30,864 --> 00:49:32,164
and I decided to focus on serving.

1144
00:49:33,166 --> 00:49:34,267
Focus on serving?

1145
00:49:34,467 --> 00:49:37,404
(So, is the Wonder Dogs' weakness
their serve reception?)

1146
00:49:37,462 --> 00:49:39,563
You scanned them
and figured everything out at once.

1147
00:49:41,708 --> 00:49:43,272
The Wonder Dogs,
having regained their confidence,

1148
00:49:43,273 --> 00:49:46,312
are aiming for their first winning streak
against a top corporate team.

1149
00:49:46,312 --> 00:49:47,746
Today's matchup
against Suwon City Hall will be covered...

1150
00:49:47,747 --> 00:49:49,214
with the commentator Lee Suk Ja.

1151
00:49:49,215 --> 00:49:51,116
- Hello.
- Nice to see you again.

1152
00:49:51,117 --> 00:49:53,185
It's a very important day.

1153
00:49:53,186 --> 00:49:56,789
The Wonder Dogs are challenging
for their first consecutive win,

1154
00:49:57,190 --> 00:49:58,457
and their opponent is Suwon City Hall,

1155
00:49:58,758 --> 00:50:00,325
a team that's gone
beyond being just the strongest,

1156
00:50:00,326 --> 00:50:03,829
showing an almost unbeatable presence
in corporate volleyball.

1157
00:50:09,881 --> 00:50:11,648
(Even from the warmup,
their spikes look dangerous.)

1158
00:50:11,650 --> 00:50:14,452
Looking at the team roster,

1159
00:50:14,953 --> 00:50:18,121
players like Park Hyeon Ju, who previously
played for the Pink Spiders,

1160
00:50:18,423 --> 00:50:21,325
and Choi Yuni, who played
for both the Altos and the Pink Spiders,

1161
00:50:21,326 --> 00:50:24,195
are very smart on the court.

1162
00:50:24,329 --> 00:50:28,232
Outside hitter Lee Yeon Jae is
also a former pro,

1163
00:50:28,233 --> 00:50:29,834
so she's an extremely powerful player.

1164
00:50:30,001 --> 00:50:33,537
Right now, this team is almost
at the level of a pro-tier lineup...

1165
00:50:33,538 --> 00:50:36,440
and should never be underestimated.

1166
00:50:39,744 --> 00:50:41,078
Hello, sir.

1167
00:50:42,180 --> 00:50:43,647
- Please be easy on us.
- I hope we have a good game.

1168
00:50:45,383 --> 00:50:47,150
I heard you came to see us train.

1169
00:50:47,252 --> 00:50:49,453
- What?
- You came by to watch our practice.

1170
00:50:49,454 --> 00:50:50,888
I left after the warm-up session.

1171
00:50:51,356 --> 00:50:53,891
I was standing on the second floor...

1172
00:50:53,892 --> 00:50:55,059
- Really?
- and left.

1173
00:50:55,927 --> 00:50:59,429
It looks like you were really confident
in the interview.

1174
00:51:01,132 --> 00:51:02,632
- You made bold claims, didn't you?
- What?

1175
00:51:04,270 --> 00:51:06,203
Anyway, I look forward to a good game.

1176
00:51:11,076 --> 00:51:13,678
As you said, the remaining games are...

1177
00:51:13,678 --> 00:51:18,448
against the pro runners-up and champions,
the top-tier teams,

1178
00:51:18,450 --> 00:51:22,720
so both the result
and the performance today must be good.

1179
00:51:22,854 --> 00:51:24,755
For the sake of the remaining games,

1180
00:51:24,756 --> 00:51:26,557
they absolutely must win this match.

1181
00:51:28,460 --> 00:51:33,698
How must Na Hee feel today,
having to face her teammates as opponents?

1182
00:51:34,199 --> 00:51:38,602
(Yesterday's teammates are today's rivals)

1183
00:51:39,153 --> 00:51:41,588
(The curtain rises on a cold battle)

1184
00:51:41,673 --> 00:51:43,440
- I'm looking forward to a good match.
- Me too.

1185
00:51:44,242 --> 00:51:46,176
Let's check the lineups for today's match.

1186
00:51:46,177 --> 00:51:49,514
Starting with Suwon City Hall,
at position one is setter Kang Bo Min,

1187
00:51:49,538 --> 00:51:51,058
outside hitter Lee Yeon Jae,

1188
00:51:51,082 --> 00:51:54,284
middle blocker Lee Ye Dam,
opposite hitter Park Hyeon Ju,

1189
00:51:54,285 --> 00:51:57,053
outside hitter Choi Yuni,
middle blocker Kim Bo Been,

1190
00:51:57,055 --> 00:51:58,255
and libero Han Su A.

1191
00:51:58,256 --> 00:51:59,790
Moving on to the Wonder Dogs,

1192
00:51:59,791 --> 00:52:01,726
at position one is setter Koo Sol,

1193
00:52:01,727 --> 00:52:04,895
outside hitter Enkhsoyol,
middle blocker Moon Myoung Hwa,

1194
00:52:05,263 --> 00:52:08,732
opposite hitter Han Song Hee,
outside hitter Pyo Seung Ju,

1195
00:52:08,868 --> 00:52:11,869
middle blocker Kim Na Hee,
and libero Koo Hye In.

1196
00:52:12,137 --> 00:52:12,870
Let's go.

1197
00:52:12,871 --> 00:52:16,674
Today, Coach Kim has put
Sol in the starting lineup,

1198
00:52:17,142 --> 00:52:19,410
and we hope she lives up to that trust.

1199
00:52:19,878 --> 00:52:21,479
- Way to go!
- Let's go!

1200
00:52:21,479 --> 00:52:24,148
(Suwon City Hall vs. the Wonder Dogs)

1201
00:52:24,616 --> 00:52:25,783
(The first set begins.)

1202
00:52:25,784 --> 00:52:27,351
- Let's go.
- Let's do this.

1203
00:52:27,352 --> 00:52:29,687
Let's get ready to take control
of the early momentum.

1204
00:52:29,687 --> 00:52:31,087
We've got this!

1205
00:52:32,324 --> 00:52:34,191
- Let's go!
- Bo Min from Suwon City Hall...

1206
00:52:34,993 --> 00:52:36,994
kicks off the first set of the game
with her serve.

1207
00:52:36,995 --> 00:52:37,795
Connect it.

1208
00:52:37,796 --> 00:52:39,664
(A shaky receive?)

1209
00:52:39,665 --> 00:52:40,631
- Slow down.
- Calm down.

1210
00:52:41,733 --> 00:52:42,666
Song Hee.

1211
00:52:43,468 --> 00:52:44,501
They kept the ball alive.

1212
00:52:45,804 --> 00:52:47,271
Yeon Jae's open spike!

1213
00:52:47,272 --> 00:52:48,305
Set it!

1214
00:52:48,306 --> 00:52:51,408
Nice set! A back toss and Enkhsoyol!

1215
00:52:52,243 --> 00:52:53,376
It's out.

1216
00:52:54,646 --> 00:52:55,879
(Trying to look nice)

1217
00:52:58,516 --> 00:52:59,516
Back to your position!

1218
00:53:00,251 --> 00:53:01,651
The score is 1 to 0.

1219
00:53:02,554 --> 00:53:03,721
In 1, 2!

1220
00:53:03,721 --> 00:53:04,688
- Hey!
- Get it.

1221
00:53:04,689 --> 00:53:06,023
(Is it a receive error?)

1222
00:53:08,460 --> 00:53:09,627
It's alright.

1223
00:53:10,161 --> 00:53:11,595
- This is no good.
- It's okay.

1224
00:53:12,397 --> 00:53:14,399
They made a serve ace
right from the start of the match.

1225
00:53:14,423 --> 00:53:15,500
Sorry.

1226
00:53:15,734 --> 00:53:17,268
Seung Ju, take a step back.

1227
00:53:17,268 --> 00:53:18,401
Take half a step back.

1228
00:53:18,670 --> 00:53:20,471
The ball is coming short,
so move back slightly.

1229
00:53:20,472 --> 00:53:21,305
Got it.

1230
00:53:26,044 --> 00:53:29,579
(Their serve-receive is shaky
from the start of the match?)

1231
00:53:29,881 --> 00:53:31,448
Serve to player number five.

1232
00:53:32,484 --> 00:53:34,418
They'll target Seung Ju.

1233
00:53:34,419 --> 00:53:37,154
Move slightly in as you play.

1234
00:53:37,589 --> 00:53:38,422
It's shaking.

1235
00:53:39,391 --> 00:53:40,358
In 1, 2.

1236
00:53:40,825 --> 00:53:41,725
Good.

1237
00:53:42,594 --> 00:53:43,994
- She dives to make the reception.
- Okay!

1238
00:53:47,165 --> 00:53:48,532
Send it wide!

1239
00:53:49,502 --> 00:53:50,868
A quick middle attack, but it's blocked.

1240
00:53:51,369 --> 00:53:52,703
It's the left side.

1241
00:53:52,704 --> 00:53:53,671
Yeon Jae.

1242
00:53:54,272 --> 00:53:55,405
Spike!

1243
00:53:55,707 --> 00:53:56,807
They defended it.

1244
00:53:58,176 --> 00:53:59,009
Song Hee's soft attack.

1245
00:53:59,744 --> 00:54:01,611
Get it!

1246
00:54:01,613 --> 00:54:02,680
Yeon Jae again.

1247
00:54:03,581 --> 00:54:05,982
Powerful spike for the point!

1248
00:54:05,984 --> 00:54:07,453
(Seung Ju conceded a point
on a touch out.)

1249
00:54:07,453 --> 00:54:09,486
Now, they are struggling again
in the early stages.

1250
00:54:09,487 --> 00:54:10,787
The score is 0 to 3.

1251
00:54:11,356 --> 00:54:13,724
One! Side out!

1252
00:54:13,925 --> 00:54:15,592
Coach Kang said...

1253
00:54:15,593 --> 00:54:18,628
they'd go for strong serves
against the Wonder Dogs.

1254
00:54:19,431 --> 00:54:20,498
Target positions 5 and 6.

1255
00:54:22,901 --> 00:54:25,102
(Position 5, position 6)

1256
00:54:28,606 --> 00:54:29,639
It's not connecting.

1257
00:54:29,641 --> 00:54:30,875
Their serve receive is wobbly.

1258
00:54:33,478 --> 00:54:34,878
A double block is executed.

1259
00:54:35,980 --> 00:54:36,880
Yeon Jae.

1260
00:54:36,881 --> 00:54:39,282
(And Yeon Jae's spike again)

1261
00:54:41,152 --> 00:54:42,319
It's a touch out.

1262
00:54:42,320 --> 00:54:43,887
- I'm sorry.
- Hey!

1263
00:54:43,888 --> 00:54:45,522
Secure the serve-receive first.

1264
00:54:45,857 --> 00:54:47,624
That was a chance ball!

1265
00:54:50,095 --> 00:54:51,662
Seriously.

1266
00:54:51,930 --> 00:54:54,398
Suwon City Hall is,
by no means, an easy opponent.

1267
00:54:54,399 --> 00:54:57,468
It's almost like facing a pro team.

1268
00:54:57,468 --> 00:54:59,569
Be prepared for a quick attack!

1269
00:55:04,542 --> 00:55:07,777
In the early stages,
our team was struggling again.

1270
00:55:08,079 --> 00:55:09,679
I was wondering what approach to take...

1271
00:55:09,681 --> 00:55:11,982
and which play direction to go for.

1272
00:55:13,485 --> 00:55:17,321
Sol, when the ball drops,
send it to the far side.

1273
00:55:17,322 --> 00:55:19,190
They'll follow, anyway.

1274
00:55:20,058 --> 00:55:21,925
One!

1275
00:55:22,760 --> 00:55:24,694
We need a side out!

1276
00:55:27,232 --> 00:55:28,666
Seung Ju makes a good receive.

1277
00:55:29,100 --> 00:55:31,202
(Following the rookie coach's instruction)

1278
00:55:31,203 --> 00:55:32,189
She sets it up.

1279
00:55:32,214 --> 00:55:33,887
(A far toss)

1280
00:55:34,843 --> 00:55:36,076
(Spike)

1281
00:55:36,076 --> 00:55:38,043
Enkhsoyol spikes!

1282
00:55:38,710 --> 00:55:41,343
Enkhsoyol gets the first point
for the Wonder Dogs.

1283
00:55:41,343 --> 00:55:43,043
(First score,
thanks to Coach Kim's strategy)

1284
00:55:44,543 --> 00:55:46,960
Koo Sol's long, wide toss...

1285
00:55:46,985 --> 00:55:49,176
made it hard for the defenders
to catch up.

1286
00:55:49,476 --> 00:55:51,910
(She uses the opening
to spike between them.)

1287
00:55:52,443 --> 00:55:55,010
(The rookie coach's strategy
for today's match)

1288
00:55:55,343 --> 00:55:57,776
(Send the ball out wide!)

1289
00:55:58,576 --> 00:56:02,010
(A deep, wide toss
to draw the middle blocker out...)

1290
00:56:03,010 --> 00:56:06,210
(then aim for the empty space!)

1291
00:56:06,876 --> 00:56:08,376
Nice toss, Sol.

1292
00:56:10,743 --> 00:56:13,276
It's time for the Wonder Dogs
to attack back.

1293
00:56:13,276 --> 00:56:14,710
Nice serve!

1294
00:56:16,210 --> 00:56:17,243
Serve!

1295
00:56:19,876 --> 00:56:20,943
Back C!

1296
00:56:20,943 --> 00:56:22,043
Lee Yeon Jae receives.

1297
00:56:22,043 --> 00:56:23,043
A back toss.

1298
00:56:23,285 --> 00:56:25,351
(A free ball right away)

1299
00:56:25,376 --> 00:56:26,543
They need a point to close the gap.

1300
00:56:26,543 --> 00:56:28,476
(Setting wide left this time)

1301
00:56:29,043 --> 00:56:30,576
(The opposing middle blocker is late.)

1302
00:56:34,076 --> 00:56:36,243
Pyo Seung Ju scores!

1303
00:56:38,610 --> 00:56:39,776
Great job!

1304
00:56:39,776 --> 00:56:42,110
- Nice hit into the gap, Seung Ju.
- Yes, Coach.

1305
00:56:42,776 --> 00:56:44,043
Good!

1306
00:56:44,068 --> 00:56:45,901
Just as Coach Kim planned!

1307
00:56:46,176 --> 00:56:49,076
(The next rally...)

1308
00:56:51,476 --> 00:56:52,910
Pyo Seung Ju scores.

1309
00:56:53,176 --> 00:56:55,176
(First set, Suwon Special City 5
: Wonder Dogs 4)

1310
00:56:56,576 --> 00:56:57,876
She sent it to the left.

1311
00:56:58,176 --> 00:56:59,476
They got the coverage.

1312
00:56:59,885 --> 00:57:01,451
The ball is on the other side.

1313
00:57:01,476 --> 00:57:02,476
Spike!

1314
00:57:02,476 --> 00:57:03,876
Defend!

1315
00:57:04,676 --> 00:57:06,210
(They dug it,
but it's a Wonder Dogs' free ball!)

1316
00:57:06,210 --> 00:57:07,376
They must use that chance!

1317
00:57:07,743 --> 00:57:08,943
(Glancing)

1318
00:57:08,943 --> 00:57:11,143
(This time, they aim for the back!)

1319
00:57:11,143 --> 00:57:13,443
A middle back attack!

1320
00:57:13,443 --> 00:57:15,243
They did it!

1321
00:57:16,276 --> 00:57:17,310
I got goosebumps.

1322
00:57:17,910 --> 00:57:20,843
That was a flawless play.

1323
00:57:20,843 --> 00:57:22,910
The team launched a powerful attack.

1324
00:57:23,576 --> 00:57:24,876
Sol!

1325
00:57:25,410 --> 00:57:26,443
Nice toss.

1326
00:57:28,110 --> 00:57:29,143
Nice toss.

1327
00:57:29,343 --> 00:57:31,610
Koo Sol may not have flashy skills,

1328
00:57:31,610 --> 00:57:35,176
but she's become much steadier.

1329
00:57:36,243 --> 00:57:37,976
(First set, Suwon Special City 6
: Wonder Dogs 5)

1330
00:57:39,010 --> 00:57:41,810
(Kim Na Hee rotates to the front row.)

1331
00:57:46,010 --> 00:57:47,876
Na Hee, block the side,
not the middle, when the ball drops.

1332
00:57:47,876 --> 00:57:49,376
- Yes, Coach.
- Not the middle.

1333
00:57:49,376 --> 00:57:50,943
(Instructing for a side block)

1334
00:57:54,410 --> 00:57:56,276
(Shaky receive!)

1335
00:57:56,276 --> 00:57:57,510
Not the middle when the ball drops.

1336
00:57:57,510 --> 00:57:59,476
(Time for the side block,
just as Coach Kim ordered.)

1337
00:57:59,776 --> 00:58:00,843
Park Hyeon Ju.

1338
00:58:00,843 --> 00:58:02,543
(Park Hyeon Ju spikes.)

1339
00:58:03,910 --> 00:58:06,076
They blocked it!

1340
00:58:07,868 --> 00:58:10,768
Kim Na Hee blocked Park Hyeon Ju's spike.

1341
00:58:10,768 --> 00:58:12,468
(Their brilliant strategy worked
perfectly.)

1342
00:58:12,468 --> 00:58:14,068
It's a tie at six to six.

1343
00:58:14,068 --> 00:58:15,468
(The score is tied in no time.)

1344
00:58:15,721 --> 00:58:19,521
(We're turning the tables now.)

1345
00:58:22,902 --> 00:58:24,068
Han Song Hee serves.

1346
00:58:26,102 --> 00:58:28,368
(Instructing the target zone)

1347
00:58:36,902 --> 00:58:38,668
She picked a good target zone.

1348
00:58:39,402 --> 00:58:40,702
Move!

1349
00:58:41,468 --> 00:58:42,668
(Glancing)

1350
00:58:42,935 --> 00:58:44,902
(I won't miss it this time!)

1351
00:58:47,902 --> 00:58:48,968
Nice!

1352
00:58:50,435 --> 00:58:51,802
Koo Sol!

1353
00:58:51,802 --> 00:58:53,368
This is her strength!

1354
00:58:54,068 --> 00:58:55,102
Great!

1355
00:58:55,102 --> 00:58:58,068
(Koo Sol takes back the lead!)

1356
00:58:59,602 --> 00:59:02,502
All setters toss the ball, but...

1357
00:59:07,735 --> 00:59:10,502
Net touch!

1358
00:59:10,835 --> 00:59:12,968
(Suwon Special City gets the point.)

1359
00:59:13,802 --> 00:59:16,135
- Are they calling a net touch?
- It's a net touch.

1360
00:59:16,160 --> 00:59:16,979
(She touched the net.)

1361
00:59:17,370 --> 00:59:18,803
- I touched the net.
- A net touch by Koo Sol.

1362
00:59:18,828 --> 00:59:20,628
- I'm sorry.
- It's a shame.

1363
00:59:20,653 --> 00:59:22,253
But the team played well.

1364
00:59:22,449 --> 00:59:23,616
It's six to seven.

1365
00:59:23,616 --> 00:59:25,282
(First set, Suwon Special City 7
: Wonder Dogs 6)

1366
00:59:25,282 --> 00:59:27,349
(Suwon Special City now serves.)

1367
00:59:28,182 --> 00:59:29,882
Park Hyeon Ju prepares to serve.

1368
00:59:29,882 --> 00:59:31,449
(Park Hyeon Ju serves.)

1369
00:59:31,449 --> 00:59:32,582
Watch carefully!

1370
00:59:34,149 --> 00:59:36,349
(Nervous)

1371
00:59:39,716 --> 00:59:40,749
A powerful serve!

1372
00:59:42,682 --> 00:59:43,682
Koo Hye In struggles,

1373
00:59:43,682 --> 00:59:44,916
- but she gets the receive.
- That's it.

1374
00:59:46,924 --> 00:59:48,557
(Pyo Seung Ju's spike)

1375
00:59:48,582 --> 00:59:49,782
She pushed it all through.

1376
00:59:50,849 --> 00:59:52,582
(Suwon Special City's second touch)

1377
00:59:57,382 --> 00:59:58,449
- A tip.
- That's it.

1378
00:59:58,449 --> 00:59:59,682
Kim Na Hee saves it.

1379
00:59:59,682 --> 01:00:00,949
(Not bad.)

1380
01:00:02,049 --> 01:00:03,116
(Han Song Hee spikes.)

1381
01:00:03,116 --> 01:00:04,316
Attack on the right!

1382
01:00:05,049 --> 01:00:06,416
It's left!

1383
01:00:07,049 --> 01:00:08,449
Suwon Special City receives the ball.

1384
01:00:08,449 --> 01:00:09,616
(To the left, just as Coach Kim said!)

1385
01:00:13,716 --> 01:00:14,982
Spike!

1386
01:00:17,549 --> 01:00:18,749
It's a touch out.

1387
01:00:18,749 --> 01:00:19,782
(Block touch out)

1388
01:00:19,782 --> 01:00:20,816
Sorry.

1389
01:00:22,116 --> 01:00:24,382
(That was so close.)

1390
01:00:24,382 --> 01:00:25,516
Nice!

1391
01:00:25,516 --> 01:00:28,349
(Suwon Special City gains the momentum.)

1392
01:00:29,949 --> 01:00:32,049
(First set, Suwon Special City 8
: Wonder Dogs 6)

1393
01:00:32,782 --> 01:00:35,182
The first technical timeout.

1394
01:00:36,882 --> 01:00:39,516
- They're setting the ball high, right?
- Yes, Coach.

1395
01:00:39,516 --> 01:00:40,882
Go and close the block.

1396
01:00:40,882 --> 01:00:43,282
- Block precisely on those high sets.
- Yes, Coach.

1397
01:00:43,282 --> 01:00:45,182
Both in timing and defense.

1398
01:00:45,182 --> 01:00:46,249
- Do you get it?
- Understood.

1399
01:00:47,716 --> 01:00:50,282
(Meanwhile, with Suwon Special City)

1400
01:00:50,649 --> 01:00:51,649
Hey!

1401
01:00:52,049 --> 01:00:54,116
Have you seen them hitting straight?

1402
01:00:54,616 --> 01:00:56,449
- No, Coach.
- Then how will you block?

1403
01:00:56,782 --> 01:00:57,882
Move closer.

1404
01:00:59,149 --> 01:01:00,816
(At the start of the first set,)

1405
01:01:01,716 --> 01:01:06,049
(the Wonder Dogs aimed
for the area between blockers.)

1406
01:01:07,382 --> 01:01:09,482
(Without a word,)

1407
01:01:11,449 --> 01:01:13,182
(Coach Kang correctly identified
their strategy!)

1408
01:01:13,182 --> 01:01:14,449
(Glancing)

1409
01:01:15,082 --> 01:01:17,916
When you move to the side to block,
leave no space in between.

1410
01:01:17,916 --> 01:01:19,516
That way, the back row can defend, right?

1411
01:01:19,516 --> 01:01:21,349
Have you seen them spike hard?

1412
01:01:22,449 --> 01:01:25,449
(They saw through the opponent's strategy
early in the set.)

1413
01:01:28,482 --> 01:01:30,416
For the Wonder Dogs,

1414
01:01:30,416 --> 01:01:32,716
- they missed some chances.
- You're right.

1415
01:01:32,716 --> 01:01:33,882
But they should close the gap.

1416
01:01:34,282 --> 01:01:35,649
In 1, 2, 3.

1417
01:01:35,649 --> 01:01:37,582
(Let's catch them up!)

1418
01:01:37,582 --> 01:01:39,949
Catch the ball!

1419
01:01:41,082 --> 01:01:43,249
(First set, Suwon Special City 9
: Wonder Dogs 7)

1420
01:01:44,116 --> 01:01:45,149
Choi Yuni serves.

1421
01:01:47,949 --> 01:01:50,449
Mine!

1422
01:01:50,882 --> 01:01:52,416
Unstable reception!

1423
01:01:54,282 --> 01:01:55,316
That can't be tossed.

1424
01:01:55,316 --> 01:01:56,316
(They sent the ball over.)

1425
01:01:56,316 --> 01:01:57,682
It's a free ball for Suwon Special City.

1426
01:01:58,582 --> 01:01:59,582
The ball goes over!

1427
01:01:59,582 --> 01:02:01,382
- She saves it.
- Hang Song Hee digs.

1428
01:02:02,416 --> 01:02:03,449
Cover!

1429
01:02:03,816 --> 01:02:04,982
(Moving swiftly)

1430
01:02:05,282 --> 01:02:06,649
(Quickly getting ready
for the hit into the gap)

1431
01:02:06,843 --> 01:02:08,158
Pyo Seung Ju sets.

1432
01:02:08,416 --> 01:02:09,649
(Enkhsoyol tips between blockers.)

1433
01:02:10,682 --> 01:02:11,749
They saved it!

1434
01:02:11,749 --> 01:02:12,782
Hit the ball!

1435
01:02:13,116 --> 01:02:14,316
The ball is near the net.

1436
01:02:16,316 --> 01:02:17,416
Attacking again!

1437
01:02:17,416 --> 01:02:18,549
It's a block out.

1438
01:02:18,549 --> 01:02:19,849
(Point lost after a touch out)

1439
01:02:21,382 --> 01:02:24,116
(They immediately blocked the plan
of hitting between blockers.)

1440
01:02:24,682 --> 01:02:26,782
(Cheering)

1441
01:02:27,116 --> 01:02:29,416
Check the short one first,
not the long one!

1442
01:02:30,849 --> 01:02:33,082
(First set, Suwon Special City 10
: Wonder Dogs 8)

1443
01:02:33,949 --> 01:02:34,949
She ran a long way.

1444
01:02:35,516 --> 01:02:36,582
A strong spike!

1445
01:02:37,516 --> 01:02:39,449
They dug it well. Time to counterattack!

1446
01:02:40,049 --> 01:02:41,182
(Seung Ju's back attack)

1447
01:02:41,182 --> 01:02:42,316
A tip in the middle!

1448
01:02:42,616 --> 01:02:43,682
The ball touches the net.

1449
01:02:45,282 --> 01:02:46,716
They must block that.

1450
01:02:47,182 --> 01:02:48,382
Enkhsoyol saved it.

1451
01:02:49,316 --> 01:02:50,316
(Attacking again)

1452
01:02:51,116 --> 01:02:52,382
Spike!

1453
01:02:53,082 --> 01:02:54,482
- They defended it.
- Hit it!

1454
01:02:54,482 --> 01:02:55,882
Hit it!

1455
01:02:57,182 --> 01:02:58,449
From the middle.

1456
01:02:58,449 --> 01:03:00,216
- She attacks, and the ball goes in.
- Right.

1457
01:03:00,216 --> 01:03:02,282
- Great.
- Nice!

1458
01:03:02,649 --> 01:03:04,282
(First set, Suwon Special City 11
: Wonder Dogs 8)

1459
01:03:04,282 --> 01:03:05,449
They move to their spots.

1460
01:03:05,449 --> 01:03:06,916
The ball is set up.

1461
01:03:07,423 --> 01:03:09,123
(Enkhsoyol is the hitter.)

1462
01:03:12,749 --> 01:03:15,616
Enkhsoyol's attack is blocked!

1463
01:03:16,549 --> 01:03:19,316
They smoothly blocked
her cross-court spike.

1464
01:03:19,316 --> 01:03:21,382
(That was easy!)

1465
01:03:21,382 --> 01:03:22,516
Nice toss!

1466
01:03:22,516 --> 01:03:24,882
The gap is four points again.

1467
01:03:25,416 --> 01:03:27,516
Enkhsoyol, which side has a low block?

1468
01:03:27,982 --> 01:03:29,916
- You can hit straight, right?
- Yes, Coach.

1469
01:03:29,916 --> 01:03:32,249
- Find the spot to hit. Got it?
- Understood.

1470
01:03:32,916 --> 01:03:35,449
(When facing a double block,)

1471
01:03:36,016 --> 01:03:39,382
(hit it straight,
aiming for the lower block!)

1472
01:03:40,082 --> 01:03:42,016
Let's do it again!

1473
01:03:42,016 --> 01:03:43,749
(Let's do it again.)

1474
01:03:43,749 --> 01:03:44,782
Take it easy.

1475
01:03:45,816 --> 01:03:47,916
(Kim Bo Been serves.)

1476
01:03:48,316 --> 01:03:50,082
- Mine!
- There you go.

1477
01:03:50,082 --> 01:03:51,194
Enkhsoyol receives it.

1478
01:03:51,982 --> 01:03:53,016
Spike!

1479
01:03:53,016 --> 01:03:54,149
They did it.

1480
01:03:54,949 --> 01:03:58,149
(Did the strategy work right away?)

1481
01:03:58,916 --> 01:04:00,049
Enkhsoyol!

1482
01:04:00,049 --> 01:04:01,516
What are you doing?

1483
01:04:01,516 --> 01:04:02,682
Enkhsoyol!

1484
01:04:02,682 --> 01:04:03,782
What are you doing?

1485
01:04:03,782 --> 01:04:06,049
Why did you hit in between again?
It should be over there!

1486
01:04:07,682 --> 01:04:11,349
(She hit into the gap again
instead of going straight!)

1487
01:04:11,682 --> 01:04:14,416
(The ball luckily went out.)

1488
01:04:14,649 --> 01:04:18,316
(But they won't always be lucky.)

1489
01:04:21,316 --> 01:04:22,649
(Gasping)

1490
01:04:23,082 --> 01:04:26,749
(Koo Sol serves.)

1491
01:04:28,049 --> 01:04:29,149
Number 3.

1492
01:04:29,682 --> 01:04:32,382
(Target zone)

1493
01:04:35,849 --> 01:04:38,616
(Correct)

1494
01:04:38,616 --> 01:04:39,949
The reception was shaky.

1495
01:04:41,282 --> 01:04:42,316
Lee Yeon Jae.

1496
01:04:43,016 --> 01:04:44,249
Dig and counterattack!

1497
01:04:44,616 --> 01:04:45,616
Spike!

1498
01:04:45,816 --> 01:04:47,916
(It's a straight shot this time!)

1499
01:04:48,249 --> 01:04:49,282
Nice.

1500
01:04:49,916 --> 01:04:50,982
Set it up!

1501
01:04:51,716 --> 01:04:53,049
(The defense struggles to cover.)

1502
01:04:53,049 --> 01:04:54,082
Are they going to hit this?

1503
01:04:54,082 --> 01:04:55,082
(Lee Yeon Jae spikes.)

1504
01:04:57,449 --> 01:04:58,716
(Out)

1505
01:05:01,049 --> 01:05:02,049
Enkhsoyol.

1506
01:05:02,282 --> 01:05:03,582
- See, I told you it would work!
- Yes, Coach!

1507
01:05:03,582 --> 01:05:06,182
Why hit into the gap? Just hit straight!

1508
01:05:07,782 --> 01:05:09,416
It's 10 to 12.

1509
01:05:09,416 --> 01:05:10,816
They closed the gap.

1510
01:05:11,816 --> 01:05:13,616
(Aim for number 3 again.)

1511
01:05:15,782 --> 01:05:17,349
Koo Sol served well too.

1512
01:05:18,316 --> 01:05:19,749
Nice serve!

1513
01:05:22,713 --> 01:05:23,882
Lee Yeon Jae saves it.

1514
01:05:24,782 --> 01:05:26,316
Spike! The ball hits the net.

1515
01:05:26,316 --> 01:05:27,716
(The set is too high!)

1516
01:05:27,716 --> 01:05:28,816
I'm sorry!

1517
01:05:32,469 --> 01:05:33,369
(After Sol saves it,)

1518
01:05:33,671 --> 01:05:36,062
(Enkhsoyol dumps it in.)

1519
01:05:41,339 --> 01:05:43,674
This is exactly
what Coach Yeon Koung talked about,

1520
01:05:43,675 --> 01:05:45,309
- the role of the taller setter!
- Right.

1521
01:05:45,444 --> 01:05:48,311
Even though Hye In's reception was stable,

1522
01:05:48,313 --> 01:05:50,080
the set was a bit too high.

1523
01:05:50,291 --> 01:05:52,492
But using her height,

1524
01:05:52,517 --> 01:05:54,752
Sol made a wonderful jump and set.

1525
01:05:54,752 --> 01:05:57,220
When the setting is made
from a higher point,

1526
01:05:57,221 --> 01:06:00,390
it's harder for the opponent to read.

1527
01:06:01,192 --> 01:06:04,127
Hey, now... Su A!

1528
01:06:04,965 --> 01:06:06,432
You had your hands up!

1529
01:06:06,464 --> 01:06:07,964
Why did you stop there?
Were you trying to shadow her?

1530
01:06:07,966 --> 01:06:08,833
No.

1531
01:06:09,367 --> 01:06:12,102
The game is still in the first set,

1532
01:06:12,103 --> 01:06:14,171
and Wonder Dogs haven't taken
the lead yet.

1533
01:06:14,172 --> 01:06:15,139
No.

1534
01:06:15,873 --> 01:06:18,775
(The powerful Enkhsoyol
steps up to serve.)

1535
01:06:19,177 --> 01:06:21,512
(She signals for her to go for Zone Two.)

1536
01:06:24,082 --> 01:06:25,215
In 1, 2, 3!

1537
01:06:25,216 --> 01:06:26,683
(Targeted zone)

1538
01:06:30,221 --> 01:06:31,822
(Powerful serve!)

1539
01:06:31,956 --> 01:06:32,956
Watch out for C!

1540
01:06:33,691 --> 01:06:34,958
(Yeon Jae's spike!)

1541
01:06:35,226 --> 01:06:36,793
Yeon Jae's spike was blocked!

1542
01:06:36,794 --> 01:06:39,362
Block!

1543
01:06:39,497 --> 01:06:41,331
- Touch!
- Yes!

1544
01:06:41,833 --> 01:06:42,766
It was a good serve, Enkhsoyol.

1545
01:06:43,368 --> 01:06:45,202
- We're doing great.
- Well done.

1546
01:06:45,470 --> 01:06:46,503
That's it!

1547
01:06:49,807 --> 01:06:51,241
Myoung Hwa, good job!

1548
01:06:52,143 --> 01:06:54,311
Myoung Hwa!

1549
01:06:54,312 --> 01:06:57,114
- Wonder Dogs' strength is their block!
- That's right.

1550
01:06:57,115 --> 01:06:59,717
It was entirely blocked!

1551
01:07:01,452 --> 01:07:04,988
Yeon Jae, angle your hit,
don't just smash it straight.

1552
01:07:04,989 --> 01:07:06,389
You'll get blocked by Myoung Hwa!

1553
01:07:06,591 --> 01:07:07,391
Sorry!

1554
01:07:07,392 --> 01:07:08,459
(Watch out for Myoung Hwa!)

1555
01:07:08,459 --> 01:07:10,205
It's a tie.
They need to turn the tables now.

1556
01:07:10,230 --> 01:07:11,361
They do.

1557
01:07:12,430 --> 01:07:15,232
(Enkhsoyol lines up for a powerful serve!)

1558
01:07:17,802 --> 01:07:19,670
(They're aiming for Zone Two again.)

1559
01:07:19,938 --> 01:07:21,206
In 1, 2, 3!

1560
01:07:21,206 --> 01:07:22,906
- Nice serve!
- Nice serve!

1561
01:07:26,010 --> 01:07:27,377
Cross-court serve!

1562
01:07:27,378 --> 01:07:28,545
Nice serve!

1563
01:07:28,846 --> 01:07:29,679
Do it!

1564
01:07:30,014 --> 01:07:31,314
Here it goes.

1565
01:07:31,449 --> 01:07:32,883
To the center.

1566
01:07:35,253 --> 01:07:37,120
Nice cross-court defense! That's it.

1567
01:07:37,255 --> 01:07:39,590
They got it! Now they have
a chance for a comeback!

1568
01:07:39,590 --> 01:07:41,291
To the right! Strong spike!

1569
01:07:46,464 --> 01:07:49,299
Wonder Dogs made a comeback!
Point by Song Hee!

1570
01:07:49,734 --> 01:07:51,368
That was a nice set, Hye In!

1571
01:07:51,369 --> 01:07:52,604
That's it!

1572
01:07:52,605 --> 01:07:53,537
(Victorious fist)

1573
01:07:53,538 --> 01:07:54,838
Good!

1574
01:07:58,242 --> 01:08:01,344
(Wait.)

1575
01:08:07,285 --> 01:08:10,387
(Enkhsoyol's strong serve)

1576
01:08:10,888 --> 01:08:13,556
(Sol's dig)

1577
01:08:14,125 --> 01:08:17,160
(Hye In's second touch)

1578
01:08:17,829 --> 01:08:20,731
(Song Hee's strong spike)

1579
01:08:20,732 --> 01:08:23,334
This is what they're truly capable of.

1580
01:08:23,534 --> 01:08:25,168
But they always start too slow.

1581
01:08:25,169 --> 01:08:26,703
That's unfortunate.

1582
01:08:27,705 --> 01:08:28,938
Hye In, that was a nice set!

1583
01:08:29,540 --> 01:08:32,435
Wonder Dogs take the lead
for the first time today.

1584
01:08:32,877 --> 01:08:35,979
Sol, that was it! Remember that spot.

1585
01:08:36,948 --> 01:08:38,148
(First set, Suwon Special City 15
: Wonder Dogs 16)

1586
01:08:38,149 --> 01:08:39,016
Serve!

1587
01:08:40,785 --> 01:08:41,551
Go!

1588
01:08:41,552 --> 01:08:42,852
You have to go!

1589
01:08:43,421 --> 01:08:44,388
Get it!

1590
01:08:44,388 --> 01:08:45,989
(Straight hit)

1591
01:08:45,990 --> 01:08:47,557
- Spike!
- That's it.

1592
01:08:49,160 --> 01:08:50,160
She digs it.

1593
01:08:52,130 --> 01:08:53,130
It grazes the net!

1594
01:08:53,965 --> 01:08:55,766
(Na Hee takes care of it safely.)

1595
01:08:55,791 --> 01:08:57,167
Sol, to the other side!

1596
01:08:57,935 --> 01:08:59,035
They set it up high.

1597
01:08:59,036 --> 01:09:00,570
(Song Hee's strong spike)

1598
01:09:00,838 --> 01:09:01,638
Cross-court attack.

1599
01:09:01,739 --> 01:09:03,234
Suwon Special City defends successfully.

1600
01:09:03,941 --> 01:09:05,141
It's passed to Yuni.

1601
01:09:05,643 --> 01:09:06,443
Go!

1602
01:09:07,412 --> 01:09:10,114
- She saves this, diving hard!
- She did it.

1603
01:09:10,114 --> 01:09:11,881
(Unbelievable)

1604
01:09:11,883 --> 01:09:13,283
That was a great dig.

1605
01:09:13,284 --> 01:09:14,484
(What's happening?)

1606
01:09:14,840 --> 01:09:15,852
To the other side.

1607
01:09:16,154 --> 01:09:17,054
This one!

1608
01:09:18,189 --> 01:09:19,322
Darn it!

1609
01:09:19,624 --> 01:09:20,691
(Starting to get confused)

1610
01:09:20,691 --> 01:09:22,058
A quick attack follows.

1611
01:09:22,193 --> 01:09:23,727
That's it!

1612
01:09:23,752 --> 01:09:25,452
A chance is given to Wonder Dogs!

1613
01:09:25,863 --> 01:09:28,364
- Seung Ju!
- Seung Ju!

1614
01:09:28,366 --> 01:09:30,100
It's a success!

1615
01:09:30,377 --> 01:09:34,447
(Wonder Dogs are now on a roll.)

1616
01:09:34,472 --> 01:09:35,605
An under toss.

1617
01:09:36,641 --> 01:09:38,456
- She digs nicely!
- Nice play.

1618
01:09:38,481 --> 01:09:39,514
She saves it.

1619
01:09:39,539 --> 01:09:40,539
(Hye In's nice dig)

1620
01:09:40,892 --> 01:09:42,392
(Sol's great set)

1621
01:09:43,545 --> 01:09:45,813
(Seung Ju's strong hit)

1622
01:09:46,221 --> 01:09:48,570
(Their plays are now connecting
organically.)

1623
01:09:48,697 --> 01:09:50,598
This point was made by the defender!

1624
01:09:50,599 --> 01:09:51,766
- Hye In!
- That's right.

1625
01:09:51,800 --> 01:09:55,202
Hye In has been showing
not only solid receiving,

1626
01:09:55,203 --> 01:09:57,971
but beautiful setting as well.

1627
01:09:58,807 --> 01:10:00,808
Even though a libero's role
usually doesn't stand out,

1628
01:10:00,809 --> 01:10:04,412
Hye In's performance truly shines.

1629
01:10:04,413 --> 01:10:05,713
(Hye In makes an amazing impression.)

1630
01:10:05,714 --> 01:10:07,381
Jump when it's right!

1631
01:10:07,382 --> 01:10:08,883
Don't jump on your own! Come on!

1632
01:10:08,884 --> 01:10:10,084
- Yes, Coach!
- Yes!

1633
01:10:11,420 --> 01:10:12,487
Hey, get it up!

1634
01:10:12,512 --> 01:10:14,413
She sets it to the left.

1635
01:10:14,898 --> 01:10:16,015
Yuni.

1636
01:10:17,124 --> 01:10:19,992
Darn it!

1637
01:10:21,930 --> 01:10:23,297
(Showing the composure
of a team in the lead.)

1638
01:10:23,298 --> 01:10:24,465
Sorry!

1639
01:10:24,600 --> 01:10:25,533
It hurts.

1640
01:10:25,968 --> 01:10:27,568
There's no point in hitting the coach.

1641
01:10:27,569 --> 01:10:29,703
That's right. She's outside the court.

1642
01:10:36,032 --> 01:10:37,132
(Suwon Special City's strategic timeout)

1643
01:10:37,133 --> 01:10:40,535
Suwon Special City's
first strategic timeout.

1644
01:10:41,171 --> 01:10:42,638
Hey!

1645
01:10:47,650 --> 01:10:49,150
I'm asking everyone in the center.

1646
01:10:49,152 --> 01:10:51,487
Did you see Sol's quick attack even once?

1647
01:10:51,855 --> 01:10:53,015
No, I didn't.

1648
01:10:53,590 --> 01:10:58,761
(The Wonder Dogs
barely attacked the middle.)

1649
01:10:59,095 --> 01:11:00,356
Then what should you do?

1650
01:11:00,463 --> 01:11:02,157
Ignore the quick attack
and go for the center.

1651
01:11:02,398 --> 01:11:05,300
You can keep her in check and follow up
on the next ball, can't you?

1652
01:11:05,301 --> 01:11:06,568
We'll go for two blockers no matter what.

1653
01:11:06,569 --> 01:11:09,371
- Okay.
- Why even stay in the middle?

1654
01:11:09,648 --> 01:11:12,550
Haven't you figured them out yet,
when the set's almost over?

1655
01:11:12,575 --> 01:11:13,535
- We will!
- We're sorry.

1656
01:11:14,143 --> 01:11:15,143
Let's go.

1657
01:11:15,144 --> 01:11:16,511
- Let's not give up!
- No!

1658
01:11:16,512 --> 01:11:17,612
- Suwon!
- Yes!

1659
01:11:18,824 --> 01:11:21,159
Since they aren't attacking the middle,

1660
01:11:21,184 --> 01:11:23,752
the coach told the blockers
to focus on the sides.

1661
01:11:23,953 --> 01:11:25,487
Count them right.

1662
01:11:25,488 --> 01:11:28,490
(How will Yeon Koung handle the change?)

1663
01:11:28,691 --> 01:11:29,624
It's 20 to 16.

1664
01:11:29,625 --> 01:11:31,493
(First set, Suwon Special City 16
: Wonder Dogs 20)

1665
01:11:33,129 --> 01:11:33,962
(Seung Ju's serve)
It's a serve.

1666
01:11:37,767 --> 01:11:38,633
Nice serve!

1667
01:11:38,634 --> 01:11:39,734
The reception was unstable.

1668
01:11:40,855 --> 01:11:41,688
(Possession switches.)
Seung Ju.

1669
01:11:42,657 --> 01:11:45,425
Na Hee steps back and to the left!
Enkhsoyol!

1670
01:11:46,480 --> 01:11:48,247
(Saved by the opponent)

1671
01:11:48,708 --> 01:11:49,641
Setting it high.

1672
01:11:50,414 --> 01:11:51,567
Yuni's hit!

1673
01:11:51,569 --> 01:11:52,869
Hye In's setting.

1674
01:11:53,304 --> 01:11:54,070
Again.
(Attack to the side)

1675
01:11:54,972 --> 01:11:55,844
Enkhsoyol!

1676
01:11:56,540 --> 01:11:58,975
(The attack breaks through the block,
but fails.)

1677
01:12:00,177 --> 01:12:00,943
Go!

1678
01:12:01,245 --> 01:12:02,879
She receives it calmly.

1679
01:12:02,880 --> 01:12:06,149
It's set up high! Enkhsoyol!

1680
01:12:06,518 --> 01:12:08,051
The defender saves it.

1681
01:12:10,254 --> 01:12:11,387
Another spike.

1682
01:12:11,622 --> 01:12:12,655
Enkhsoyol.

1683
01:12:13,017 --> 01:12:15,318
(Another chance to attack is here!)

1684
01:12:15,343 --> 01:12:18,245
(Sol always goes for the sides.)

1685
01:12:18,671 --> 01:12:21,074
(Will it be the same this time?)

1686
01:12:25,072 --> 01:12:25,838
Sol!

1687
01:12:26,540 --> 01:12:28,307
It's a success!

1688
01:12:31,879 --> 01:12:33,012
(That's it.)

1689
01:12:33,013 --> 01:12:34,180
- Quick attack.
- Right.

1690
01:12:35,516 --> 01:12:36,850
Nice!

1691
01:12:37,584 --> 01:12:40,820
(Earlier during the timeout)

1692
01:12:41,689 --> 01:12:43,356
You can focus more on the middle.

1693
01:12:43,357 --> 01:12:44,891
Keep that in mind.

1694
01:12:44,892 --> 01:12:46,526
It's either a middle quick attack
or a back attack.

1695
01:12:46,527 --> 01:12:49,329
- Their blocker will go for the side.
- Okay.

1696
01:12:50,531 --> 01:12:52,198
(This is how Sol utilizes the strategy.)

1697
01:12:52,700 --> 01:12:56,036
(I'll handle it
instead of the middle blocker.)

1698
01:12:56,036 --> 01:12:57,737
Sol used to play...

1699
01:12:57,738 --> 01:13:00,440
- as a middle blocker as well.
- That's right.

1700
01:13:00,441 --> 01:13:02,509
- It's not totally unfamiliar to her.
- Exactly.

1701
01:13:03,577 --> 01:13:06,212
(First set, Suwon Special City 17
: Wonder Dogs 22)

1702
01:13:06,647 --> 01:13:09,249
(Yuni's serve)

1703
01:13:12,553 --> 01:13:13,620
The reception was unstable.

1704
01:13:13,821 --> 01:13:14,821
It's okay!

1705
01:13:14,822 --> 01:13:16,456
(They set it to the side hastily.)

1706
01:13:17,358 --> 01:13:19,347
(The side is defended as always.)

1707
01:13:20,160 --> 01:13:20,960
She moves.

1708
01:13:21,295 --> 01:13:22,495
(Nice dig by Hye In)

1709
01:13:22,496 --> 01:13:24,067
- The defense was successful.
- That was a nice move.

1710
01:13:25,174 --> 01:13:26,836
The ball goes to Na Hee, grazing the net.

1711
01:13:27,610 --> 01:13:28,944
You can focus more on the middle.

1712
01:13:30,486 --> 01:13:32,120
Sol!

1713
01:13:32,145 --> 01:13:33,212
It's out!

1714
01:13:33,416 --> 01:13:34,516
Judge!

1715
01:13:34,517 --> 01:13:35,726
(What's the referee's call?)

1716
01:13:37,168 --> 01:13:38,935
(Wonder Dogs' score!)

1717
01:13:38,937 --> 01:13:39,904
Nice!

1718
01:13:40,271 --> 01:13:41,972
Well done.

1719
01:13:42,207 --> 01:13:44,708
It's touch out!

1720
01:13:44,709 --> 01:13:47,377
The ball went out
after touching Yeon Jae's fingers.

1721
01:13:47,378 --> 01:13:49,012
(Touch out off the blocker's fingers)

1722
01:13:50,281 --> 01:13:51,147
Sol is doing great.

1723
01:13:51,149 --> 01:13:53,150
- She's amazing.
- Sol is good, right?

1724
01:13:53,524 --> 01:13:55,258
I can see...

1725
01:13:55,486 --> 01:13:58,701
- Sol's confidence is at its peak.
- That's right.

1726
01:13:59,791 --> 01:14:00,991
(She's dominating the court today.)

1727
01:14:00,992 --> 01:14:02,359
- Thank you.
- Sorry!

1728
01:14:03,361 --> 01:14:07,798
(But she is the biggest underdog...)

1729
01:14:10,668 --> 01:14:14,004
(among these 14 underdogs.)

1730
01:14:14,592 --> 01:14:17,160
I realized that I wasn't good enough,

1731
01:14:17,162 --> 01:14:18,721
so I decided to work harder to improve.

1732
01:14:19,931 --> 01:14:23,467
(The first thing this underdog setter
chose to do was...)

1733
01:14:23,468 --> 01:14:25,135
(to steal one volleyball.)

1734
01:14:25,136 --> 01:14:26,336
Let me take this one.

1735
01:14:28,106 --> 01:14:31,041
I try to familiarize myself with the ball,

1736
01:14:31,042 --> 01:14:33,410
bouncing it against the wall...

1737
01:14:33,411 --> 01:14:35,712
and playing with it in my room.

1738
01:14:35,713 --> 01:14:38,281
That's how I wake up my sense
for the ball.

1739
01:14:38,283 --> 01:14:40,084
I do it because I think it's necessary.

1740
01:14:40,552 --> 01:14:43,220
Coach Kim doesn't know
what you've been doing.

1741
01:14:44,122 --> 01:14:45,355
How does that make you feel?

1742
01:14:45,557 --> 01:14:47,024
Well, actually...

1743
01:14:47,258 --> 01:14:49,693
It doesn't matter
whether she knows or not.

1744
01:14:49,694 --> 01:14:53,864
I'm doing this because I lack skill.

1745
01:14:54,632 --> 01:14:57,901
I believe if I keep doing my job,

1746
01:14:59,437 --> 01:15:00,804
my chance will eventually come.

1747
01:15:01,639 --> 01:15:02,939
Sol!

1748
01:15:03,541 --> 01:15:07,177
Seung Ju!

1749
01:15:07,812 --> 01:15:08,979
(Nice set!)

1750
01:15:08,980 --> 01:15:10,147
Sol!

1751
01:15:10,172 --> 01:15:12,378
(Her hidden effort is paying off.)

1752
01:15:12,917 --> 01:15:13,517
(Clapping)

1753
01:15:14,486 --> 01:15:15,186
Good.

1754
01:15:15,186 --> 01:15:18,522
(She finally proves herself to the coach.)

1755
01:15:18,523 --> 01:15:21,692
Sol said she's figured out how to set now.

1756
01:15:21,693 --> 01:15:23,152
That gives me a headache.

1757
01:15:23,795 --> 01:15:24,828
That's what she said.

1758
01:15:24,829 --> 01:15:26,673
Why did she figure it out now,
all of a sudden?

1759
01:15:26,698 --> 01:15:28,365
Enkhsoyol, go for this side!

1760
01:15:28,833 --> 01:15:31,727
Enkhsoyol, when they attack,
go for this zone.

1761
01:15:32,534 --> 01:15:33,034
Yes.

1762
01:15:37,269 --> 01:15:38,335
Enkhsoyol.

1763
01:15:38,360 --> 01:15:39,294
Sol.

1764
01:15:39,294 --> 01:15:40,694
(Sticking to the plan)

1765
01:15:40,694 --> 01:15:42,394
Enkhsoyol!

1766
01:15:42,394 --> 01:15:44,060
- That was great.
- Yes.

1767
01:15:44,927 --> 01:15:45,860
Thank you.

1768
01:15:48,771 --> 01:15:50,804
Volleyball is my life, you know.

1769
01:15:50,804 --> 01:15:54,004
I want to give it my all,
as much as I can.

1770
01:15:54,591 --> 01:15:57,125
It is now the set point
for the Wonder Dogs.

1771
01:15:58,804 --> 01:16:00,371
Short serve!

1772
01:16:00,904 --> 01:16:02,258
Watch the front!

1773
01:16:03,538 --> 01:16:04,538
Watch the net!

1774
01:16:04,538 --> 01:16:06,271
Toss it to Song Hee.

1775
01:16:06,804 --> 01:16:09,004
Myoung Hwa!

1776
01:16:09,004 --> 01:16:10,971
(Fake signaling to Myoung Hwa)

1777
01:16:11,138 --> 01:16:12,004
Myoung Hwa!
(Myoung Hwa?)

1778
01:16:16,204 --> 01:16:17,538
(The receive was a bit shaky,)

1779
01:16:19,738 --> 01:16:21,738
(but the set is on point!)

1780
01:16:22,904 --> 01:16:23,838
(Song Hee spikes.)

1781
01:16:23,838 --> 01:16:25,571
She spikes!

1782
01:16:25,571 --> 01:16:27,838
Set one, 25 to 19.

1783
01:16:27,838 --> 01:16:29,571
Wonder Dogs win the set.

1784
01:16:31,038 --> 01:16:32,738
(Second set timeout)

1785
01:16:32,738 --> 01:16:33,938
- Hyeon Ju.
- Yes?

1786
01:16:33,938 --> 01:16:35,591
How are you going to avoid their block?

1787
01:16:36,604 --> 01:16:39,504
(Getting nervous)

1788
01:16:39,504 --> 01:16:41,971
Sol is tall,
so when she's making a big movement,

1789
01:16:42,271 --> 01:16:44,099
she doesn't spike with her left hand.

1790
01:16:44,524 --> 01:16:45,634
She uses her right hand.

1791
01:16:45,971 --> 01:16:48,571
But you weren't blocking
when she raised her left hand.

1792
01:16:48,571 --> 01:16:49,804
And vice versa.

1793
01:16:49,804 --> 01:16:51,471
- What were you thinking?
- Sorry, coach.

1794
01:16:53,338 --> 01:16:54,971
- You get it, right?
- Yes, coach.

1795
01:16:56,238 --> 01:16:58,538
(Refocusing mentally once again...)

1796
01:16:59,171 --> 01:17:02,771
(to win the second set)

1797
01:17:03,238 --> 01:17:05,638
Set one, 25 to 19.

1798
01:17:05,638 --> 01:17:08,071
Wonder Dogs turned it around
and took the set.

1799
01:17:08,071 --> 01:17:10,638
We hope they can carry this momentum
into the second set.

1800
01:17:11,613 --> 01:17:13,046
Right before the game,

1801
01:17:13,071 --> 01:17:15,871
I did a little image training.

1802
01:17:16,471 --> 01:17:21,637
(Sol was on fire in the first set.)

1803
01:17:23,004 --> 01:17:25,504
It's a game we've all waited for,

1804
01:17:25,971 --> 01:17:28,637
and if we believe in ourselves
that we can do it,

1805
01:17:28,637 --> 01:17:30,379
I think we can put on a good game.

1806
01:17:32,004 --> 01:17:32,837
Sol.

1807
01:17:32,837 --> 01:17:34,237
(Signaling serve target)

1808
01:17:34,237 --> 01:17:35,404
Oh, okay.

1809
01:17:36,237 --> 01:17:38,671
(Target zone)

1810
01:17:38,904 --> 01:17:39,871
Set two begins.

1811
01:17:39,871 --> 01:17:40,904
(Sol's serve)

1812
01:17:42,104 --> 01:17:43,604
Come on.

1813
01:17:45,404 --> 01:17:46,737
(Targeted serve failed)

1814
01:17:47,137 --> 01:17:48,337
(After a stable set,)

1815
01:17:48,337 --> 01:17:49,204
(a spike)

1816
01:17:49,537 --> 01:17:50,404
Yeon Jae spikes.

1817
01:17:51,171 --> 01:17:52,171
They saved it.

1818
01:17:52,196 --> 01:17:53,172
(Onto the other side)

1819
01:17:54,537 --> 01:17:55,671
They're attacking again.

1820
01:17:55,696 --> 01:17:56,583
(Another attack)

1821
01:17:58,004 --> 01:17:58,871
Spike!

1822
01:18:00,104 --> 01:18:01,071
It's out!

1823
01:18:01,637 --> 01:18:02,837
It's in!

1824
01:18:03,437 --> 01:18:04,337
Was that out?

1825
01:18:04,771 --> 01:18:07,304
- They call out.
- The ball was out.

1826
01:18:07,304 --> 01:18:08,804
- Nice.
- Yes!

1827
01:18:10,037 --> 01:18:11,137
Watch where you serve, Sol!

1828
01:18:11,137 --> 01:18:12,404
There, short serve.

1829
01:18:13,004 --> 01:18:14,004
(Giving her a look)

1830
01:18:17,271 --> 01:18:19,871
(Signaling the next serve target)

1831
01:18:19,871 --> 01:18:22,571
Watch the right side!

1832
01:18:22,804 --> 01:18:23,971
(Reset and focus)

1833
01:18:23,971 --> 01:18:24,971
The score is one to zero.

1834
01:18:26,304 --> 01:18:27,237
Hey!

1835
01:18:28,337 --> 01:18:29,604
(Giving her a look again)

1836
01:18:31,204 --> 01:18:32,337
(Flies off and straight out)

1837
01:18:32,704 --> 01:18:35,504
(Each team made one error)

1838
01:18:35,504 --> 01:18:36,337
Sorry.

1839
01:18:36,971 --> 01:18:38,304
She's swinging wildly.

1840
01:18:38,537 --> 01:18:40,771
She's trying to do something, I guess.

1841
01:18:40,771 --> 01:18:42,304
(Unbelievable)

1842
01:18:43,304 --> 01:18:45,204
Stick to the basics.

1843
01:18:45,637 --> 01:18:46,655
Don't try to overplay it.

1844
01:18:47,371 --> 01:18:48,971
Yeon Jae's serve.

1845
01:18:50,837 --> 01:18:52,704
(The ball is set for Song Hee.)

1846
01:18:52,704 --> 01:18:54,504
Nice toss!

1847
01:18:54,871 --> 01:18:56,671
(And attacking...)

1848
01:18:56,671 --> 01:18:57,971
(in perfect rhythm)

1849
01:18:58,979 --> 01:19:00,012
Song Hee!

1850
01:19:00,037 --> 01:19:01,404
A block out point!

1851
01:19:01,804 --> 01:19:04,004
(Screaming in relief)

1852
01:19:04,904 --> 01:19:05,971
Sorry for the catch.

1853
01:19:05,971 --> 01:19:08,504
Go, Song Hee!

1854
01:19:09,071 --> 01:19:11,071
Is there something I'm missing over there?

1855
01:19:11,071 --> 01:19:12,637
Why do you keep going there?

1856
01:19:13,504 --> 01:19:15,671
With the first set win,

1857
01:19:15,671 --> 01:19:17,971
the players seem to be gaining...

1858
01:19:17,971 --> 01:19:20,404
- confidence in their play.
- That's right.

1859
01:19:20,404 --> 01:19:22,337
Sol's set is much more powerful now,

1860
01:19:22,337 --> 01:19:23,904
and it's fast too.

1861
01:19:24,904 --> 01:19:27,071
(Second set, Suwon Special City 2
: Wonder Dogs 2)

1862
01:19:27,971 --> 01:19:30,137
- Watch out for a floater serve.
- Okay.

1863
01:19:30,604 --> 01:19:32,504
- Short serve!
- Watch out for the short serve!

1864
01:19:33,437 --> 01:19:34,771
(Watching closely)

1865
01:19:34,771 --> 01:19:36,171
Aim for one.

1866
01:19:36,704 --> 01:19:38,504
- Did you hear me?
- Yes.

1867
01:19:39,071 --> 01:19:41,437
(Enkhsoyol is her target.)

1868
01:19:42,004 --> 01:19:42,804
Serve!
One, two!

1869
01:19:44,937 --> 01:19:45,871
That's it!

1870
01:19:45,871 --> 01:19:47,537
- My!
- That's it!

1871
01:19:48,171 --> 01:19:49,471
A single set!

1872
01:19:50,437 --> 01:19:51,971
- Hyeon Ju!
- Hit it!

1873
01:19:54,037 --> 01:19:55,971
(The minute Hyeon Ju jumps up,)

1874
01:19:56,437 --> 01:19:58,904
(Myoung Hwa moves in the fastest motion.)

1875
01:19:58,904 --> 01:20:01,271
- Hyeon Ju!
- Hit it!

1876
01:20:01,271 --> 01:20:03,137
(Blocked)

1877
01:20:03,137 --> 01:20:04,437
Hyeon Ju spikes!

1878
01:20:04,437 --> 01:20:05,904
They blocked it!

1879
01:20:05,904 --> 01:20:07,837
Myoung Hwa!

1880
01:20:07,837 --> 01:20:10,104
Her block is high. Really high.

1881
01:20:10,104 --> 01:20:11,537
Myoung Hwa, good job.

1882
01:20:13,137 --> 01:20:15,037
Look at what happened.

1883
01:20:15,037 --> 01:20:18,137
When she blocks a predictable ball,

1884
01:20:18,137 --> 01:20:20,037
no one can break
through Myoung Hwa's block.

1885
01:20:20,037 --> 01:20:20,837
Absolutely.
(A perfectly timed block)

1886
01:20:23,504 --> 01:20:25,237
Myoung Hwa, good job.

1887
01:20:25,737 --> 01:20:29,404
I believe this is a tactic
Coach Yeon Koung designed.

1888
01:20:30,471 --> 01:20:32,837
(Video prep for the match
against Suwon City Hall)

1889
01:20:33,037 --> 01:20:35,937
We are going to block with both hands.

1890
01:20:35,937 --> 01:20:39,404
We are going to block with the left hand
for player number 19.

1891
01:20:39,771 --> 01:20:42,504
(Targeted blocking tactics
for each attacker)

1892
01:20:42,871 --> 01:20:45,471
(The reason Myoung Hwa could
block at such speed)

1893
01:20:46,304 --> 01:20:49,071
(For Hyeon Ju, block between both hands)

1894
01:20:49,871 --> 01:20:52,937
(The tactic worked beautifully.)

1895
01:20:54,137 --> 01:20:55,037
Hyeon Ju!

1896
01:20:55,837 --> 01:20:58,104
Don't try to be cool and spike it across.

1897
01:20:58,104 --> 01:20:58,904
Yes, coach.

1898
01:21:01,904 --> 01:21:04,071
(Serve queen serves, riding the momentum.)

1899
01:21:05,612 --> 01:21:07,879
(Yuni is getting ready to attack)

1900
01:21:07,904 --> 01:21:09,831
She drops a tip in Zone Three
from time to time.

1901
01:21:10,637 --> 01:21:13,204
(You're going to tip into Zone Three,
aren't you?)

1902
01:21:14,104 --> 01:21:15,171
(Yes, I am.)

1903
01:21:15,704 --> 01:21:16,571
Wait, save it!
(No way.)

1904
01:21:17,437 --> 01:21:18,404
Come on.
Yes.

1905
01:21:19,704 --> 01:21:20,571
(Getting ready to attack)

1906
01:21:20,571 --> 01:21:21,937
Enkhsoyol from the left.

1907
01:21:21,937 --> 01:21:23,137
Jumping up and tipping!

1908
01:21:23,137 --> 01:21:24,404
(Seung Ju's tip)

1909
01:21:24,871 --> 01:21:27,204
(Hyeon Ju is coming again!)

1910
01:21:30,243 --> 01:21:32,610
We are going to block with space
between both hands.

1911
01:21:33,181 --> 01:21:36,271
(Will it work again this time?)

1912
01:21:37,971 --> 01:21:40,671
(The Wonder coach's tactics are working
every time!)

1913
01:21:41,037 --> 01:21:43,271
Hyeon Ju spikes, and it's blocked!

1914
01:21:43,271 --> 01:21:45,337
Another block point!

1915
01:21:45,337 --> 01:21:47,804
There's no room for Hyeon Ju to attack.

1916
01:21:50,437 --> 01:21:52,871
If they block
both the left and right sides,

1917
01:21:52,871 --> 01:21:56,604
the Suwon Special City attackers,

1918
01:21:56,604 --> 01:21:59,037
- must be feeling intimidated.
- That's right.

1919
01:22:00,104 --> 01:22:03,671
(Riding the momentum, Myoung Hwa serves.)

1920
01:22:04,304 --> 01:22:06,504
(So reliable)

1921
01:22:07,037 --> 01:22:09,271
(Here comes the serving queen.)

1922
01:22:16,204 --> 01:22:23,237
Direct attack on the free ball!

1923
01:22:24,371 --> 01:22:26,237
Myoung Hwa!

1924
01:22:26,704 --> 01:22:28,637
That was a point off the serve.

1925
01:22:28,637 --> 01:22:29,804
Yes, indeed.

1926
01:22:29,829 --> 01:22:34,429
Myoung Hwa was scolded for not hitting
65 kilometers per hour on her serve.

1927
01:22:35,271 --> 01:22:37,437
- But look now!
- Yes.

1928
01:22:37,437 --> 01:22:41,271
She's one of the players
who has the strongest serving skills.

1929
01:22:44,637 --> 01:22:46,304
(Out)

1930
01:22:46,637 --> 01:22:47,804
Darn it!

1931
01:22:48,704 --> 01:22:51,071
I guess we jinxed it.

1932
01:22:51,071 --> 01:22:52,204
Yes, sorry.

1933
01:22:52,204 --> 01:22:53,704
We should hold back.

1934
01:22:55,537 --> 01:22:57,704
(Stomping in frustration)

1935
01:22:59,904 --> 01:23:01,537
I missed it!

1936
01:23:02,204 --> 01:23:05,671
(Second set, Suwon Special City 3
: Wonder Dogs 7)

1937
01:23:05,971 --> 01:23:07,604
(The game continues.)

1938
01:23:08,537 --> 01:23:11,371
Seung Ju, she's running!

1939
01:23:11,704 --> 01:23:13,804
(Seung Ju blocks on Yeon Koung's advice.)

1940
01:23:13,804 --> 01:23:14,637
That's it!

1941
01:23:16,871 --> 01:23:17,804
A standing spike!

1942
01:23:18,371 --> 01:23:19,537
It's a straight!

1943
01:23:20,037 --> 01:23:21,971
We should block with the left hand, right?

1944
01:23:23,571 --> 01:23:25,671
(Sol blocks with the left hand.)

1945
01:23:26,004 --> 01:23:29,537
Yes, that's it!

1946
01:23:29,537 --> 01:23:31,171
Point off the block!

1947
01:23:31,171 --> 01:23:32,671
Sol!

1948
01:23:33,671 --> 01:23:35,004
(So satisfying)

1949
01:23:35,004 --> 01:23:36,371
Sol, nice one!

1950
01:23:36,804 --> 01:23:39,537
There's hardly a player
who hasn't felt the ball now.

1951
01:23:39,537 --> 01:23:42,337
Every single player is participating
in blocking,

1952
01:23:42,637 --> 01:23:45,837
Suwon Special City players must be
feeling afraid to hit the ball over.

1953
01:23:46,337 --> 01:23:47,671
Now, the score is 8 to 3,

1954
01:23:47,671 --> 01:23:50,437
and we are in the first technical timeout
of the second set.

1955
01:23:51,271 --> 01:23:53,771
The sides aren't helping the attack
at all.

1956
01:23:55,171 --> 01:23:57,171
Do you want to go in?
Want to switch with Min Ji?

1957
01:23:57,171 --> 01:23:58,071
- No.
- You sure?

1958
01:24:01,004 --> 01:24:02,671
Look at Na Hee.

1959
01:24:02,671 --> 01:24:04,404
Na Hee tends to spread her arms
for blocking.

1960
01:24:04,737 --> 01:24:06,404
So why aim and hit?

1961
01:24:06,404 --> 01:24:07,837
Just hit between the gap.

1962
01:24:08,637 --> 01:24:13,404
(New strategy:
Break through Na Hee's block)

1963
01:24:13,904 --> 01:24:17,104
Wonder Dogs should
forget the score difference right now...

1964
01:24:17,104 --> 01:24:18,337
and keep pushing.

1965
01:24:18,337 --> 01:24:19,537
(Attack Na Hee to regain the flow)

1966
01:24:20,037 --> 01:24:21,204
(Will it work?)

1967
01:24:21,204 --> 01:24:22,171
One, two.

1968
01:24:24,571 --> 01:24:25,837
The receive was a bit shaky.

1969
01:24:26,904 --> 01:24:28,229
They send it back over.

1970
01:24:29,971 --> 01:24:31,537
(Spike)

1971
01:24:31,937 --> 01:24:32,937
They blocked it well.

1972
01:24:35,604 --> 01:24:37,937
(Again, Yeon Jae attacks)

1973
01:24:38,537 --> 01:24:41,637
(Smack it in between Na Hee's hands.)

1974
01:24:42,404 --> 01:24:45,271
(Will they be able to break
through Na Hee's block?)

1975
01:24:47,771 --> 01:24:49,404
(They broke it!)

1976
01:24:49,404 --> 01:24:50,437
Hit it!

1977
01:24:52,304 --> 01:24:53,337
Nice!

1978
01:24:54,937 --> 01:24:57,904
- Spike!
- And it's out!

1979
01:24:57,904 --> 01:25:00,371
- She pulled her arms down.
- She did.

1980
01:25:00,371 --> 01:25:04,937
She understands
the opponent's plays perfectly,

1981
01:25:04,937 --> 01:25:06,937
and the timing
to pull down was also perfect.

1982
01:25:06,937 --> 01:25:08,737
She raised her hands, and when she spiked,

1983
01:25:08,737 --> 01:25:09,737
she pulled down her arms.

1984
01:25:10,537 --> 01:25:11,971
No change, Sol?

1985
01:25:11,971 --> 01:25:14,937
(Na Hee's counterattack)

1986
01:25:14,937 --> 01:25:16,304
Hyo Rim!

1987
01:25:17,237 --> 01:25:20,171
(Signaling to setter)

1988
01:25:20,471 --> 01:25:22,404
(Okay.)

1989
01:25:22,771 --> 01:25:25,004
(Seung Ju's serve)

1990
01:25:27,971 --> 01:25:30,137
(Setter Hyo Rim's surprise back set)

1991
01:25:30,161 --> 01:25:31,928
(A Successful quick attack on the move)

1992
01:25:32,197 --> 01:25:33,063
Great!

1993
01:25:33,064 --> 01:25:35,399
(A perfect play of the setter
and the middle blocker)

1994
01:25:36,034 --> 01:25:37,634
(Satisfied)

1995
01:25:37,635 --> 01:25:38,668
Wait first.

1996
01:25:38,693 --> 01:25:40,373
(Satisfied)

1997
01:25:41,288 --> 01:25:42,088
You were too late.

1998
01:25:42,088 --> 01:25:44,790
It was a back A with no feinting move,
so why didn't you jump?

1999
01:25:45,665 --> 01:25:46,898
It's my mistake.

2000
01:25:47,060 --> 01:25:48,414
Come on.

2001
01:25:48,562 --> 01:25:52,464
It looks like Suwon Special City started
making more quick attack attempts.

2002
01:25:52,465 --> 01:25:55,400
Since the blocking is set high,

2003
01:25:55,402 --> 01:25:58,037
the only option they have is
quick attacks.

2004
01:25:58,204 --> 01:25:59,771
Wait for the block...

2005
01:26:00,473 --> 01:26:03,108
and jump at the right time.

2006
01:26:03,109 --> 01:26:05,711
Stay quick on your rhythm,
find your hitting point right away,

2007
01:26:05,745 --> 01:26:06,879
and swing fast.

2008
01:26:06,880 --> 01:26:07,646
- Okay.
- Okay.

2009
01:26:08,181 --> 01:26:10,550
(A tough and seasoned Coach Kang)

2010
01:26:10,551 --> 01:26:11,717
Enkhsoyol.

2011
01:26:11,918 --> 01:26:13,152
Inside.

2012
01:26:13,153 --> 01:26:14,487
Watch out for their feints.

2013
01:26:14,488 --> 01:26:15,821
- Inside.
- Okay.

2014
01:26:16,690 --> 01:26:17,823
Let's go right away!

2015
01:26:17,824 --> 01:26:20,159
(This time, the plan is
an off-speed feint.)

2016
01:26:20,493 --> 01:26:21,660
Serve!

2017
01:26:21,728 --> 01:26:23,095
The score is 9 to 6.

2018
01:26:25,465 --> 01:26:26,432
- Mine.
- Get it.

2019
01:26:28,268 --> 01:26:31,303
(The set goes toward Enkhsoyol.)

2020
01:26:31,304 --> 01:26:32,437
Enkhsoyol!

2021
01:26:33,106 --> 01:26:35,273
It's an effective block.

2022
01:26:35,298 --> 01:26:35,952
(Nodding)

2023
01:26:37,711 --> 01:26:38,778
(And a tip by Hyeon Ju)

2024
01:26:38,778 --> 01:26:39,878
Slow down.

2025
01:26:40,013 --> 01:26:41,480
There she goes.

2026
01:26:43,316 --> 01:26:44,116
Feint!

2027
01:26:44,117 --> 01:26:47,086
(Now is the perfect moment for a feint.)

2028
01:26:49,445 --> 01:26:51,657
She pushed it in precisely.

2029
01:26:52,659 --> 01:26:55,594
- Enkhsoyol, that was a nice tip.
- Good job.

2030
01:26:56,788 --> 01:27:00,691
(She's been emphasizing the tip play
toward Zone Three since the first game.)

2031
01:27:01,534 --> 01:27:06,972
(But something feels different this time.)

2032
01:27:08,216 --> 01:27:11,085
(The rookie coach's
customized offensive plan for Enkhsoyol)

2033
01:27:11,611 --> 01:27:16,815
(A powerful straight spike
toward the lower side of the block)

2034
01:27:17,484 --> 01:27:19,618
(Then, the defense naturally shifts
toward the line.)

2035
01:27:19,653 --> 01:27:21,220
Then, where should you aim?

2036
01:27:21,354 --> 01:27:22,954
Inside, of course.

2037
01:27:23,623 --> 01:27:26,625
(A feint attack to the open middle)

2038
01:27:27,327 --> 01:27:28,260
Feint!

2039
01:27:28,962 --> 01:27:31,730
(Perfect execution)

2040
01:27:31,731 --> 01:27:34,199
Number 3 Enkhsoyol targeted the ball
to Zone 3.

2041
01:27:34,300 --> 01:27:35,467
Enkhsoyol, do it like this one.

2042
01:27:35,662 --> 01:27:38,163
You hit, and the right defender covers.
What do you do?

2043
01:27:38,477 --> 01:27:40,845
- Use a feint like this.
- Yes.

2044
01:27:41,600 --> 01:27:44,202
- A feint.
- Let's make it happen!

2045
01:27:45,484 --> 01:27:46,818
Na Hee is the server.

2046
01:27:49,315 --> 01:27:50,815
- Go get it.
- Okay.

2047
01:27:50,850 --> 01:27:52,184
(The set goes long.)

2048
01:27:52,185 --> 01:27:53,385
Over the net!

2049
01:27:54,387 --> 01:27:55,320
Yes!

2050
01:27:57,490 --> 01:27:58,523
That was great.

2051
01:27:59,059 --> 01:28:00,559
My serve!

2052
01:28:00,560 --> 01:28:04,363
Myoung Hwa is indeed very tall!

2053
01:28:05,298 --> 01:28:07,900
(I knew it.)

2054
01:28:07,901 --> 01:28:09,869
I'm sorry.

2055
01:28:10,203 --> 01:28:11,770
It's my fault. I'm sorry.

2056
01:28:13,606 --> 01:28:14,940
(Sighing)

2057
01:28:14,941 --> 01:28:16,257
The score is 11 to 6.

2058
01:28:18,011 --> 01:28:20,212
(Target the serve at Zone Four.)

2059
01:28:20,213 --> 01:28:20,913
Okay.

2060
01:28:22,682 --> 01:28:24,216
Nice serve, Na Hee.

2061
01:28:28,268 --> 01:28:29,671
The serve receive is unstable.

2062
01:28:30,596 --> 01:28:31,429
Wait.

2063
01:28:31,728 --> 01:28:33,262
It's a chance ball. Hit it!

2064
01:28:33,497 --> 01:28:34,697
Close in!

2065
01:28:34,965 --> 01:28:37,234
(But the ball failed to clear the net.)

2066
01:28:37,701 --> 01:28:38,801
- Hit it!
- Hit it!

2067
01:28:39,269 --> 01:28:40,035
Mine.

2068
01:28:40,037 --> 01:28:41,504
You've got this.

2069
01:28:42,339 --> 01:28:45,174
A chance for a counterattack
after an effective block.

2070
01:28:45,876 --> 01:28:47,143
There she goes.

2071
01:28:47,586 --> 01:28:49,932
- Use a feint like this.
- Okay.

2072
01:28:53,083 --> 01:28:53,983
Feint!

2073
01:28:53,984 --> 01:28:56,719
(Another tip point to Zone Three.)

2074
01:28:57,621 --> 01:28:59,121
Zone Three!

2075
01:28:59,224 --> 01:29:01,423
She read the open space perfectly.

2076
01:29:01,658 --> 01:29:04,493
In the first game, the coach kept
emphasizing Zone Three.

2077
01:29:05,195 --> 01:29:08,597
(Our Enkhsoyol has changed!)

2078
01:29:08,865 --> 01:29:10,465
Enkhsoyol!

2079
01:29:10,901 --> 01:29:12,602
She's improved a lot.

2080
01:29:13,870 --> 01:29:16,772
(Proud of her)

2081
01:29:17,374 --> 01:29:20,209
Yeon Jae can't handle the feint.

2082
01:29:23,480 --> 01:29:25,247
Let's push it further.

2083
01:29:25,248 --> 01:29:26,849
Just perfect now.

2084
01:29:26,850 --> 01:29:29,285
Check out the middle, Enkhsoyol.

2085
01:29:29,486 --> 01:29:30,252
Okay.

2086
01:29:31,989 --> 01:29:34,157
(Moving in)

2087
01:29:37,127 --> 01:29:37,960
Hit it.

2088
01:29:37,961 --> 01:29:40,196
(Suwon Special City's
quick attack attempt)

2089
01:29:46,503 --> 01:29:48,871
Another point scored here.

2090
01:29:48,872 --> 01:29:50,407
(They took the middle!)

2091
01:29:50,408 --> 01:29:52,341
Myoung Hwa!

2092
01:29:52,877 --> 01:29:54,778
Since there are two blockers
on the other side,

2093
01:29:54,779 --> 01:29:57,547
Enkhsoyol also moved to the center,

2094
01:29:57,548 --> 01:30:00,316
looking for the optimal spot
to start her attack.

2095
01:30:02,519 --> 01:30:05,054
(Enkhsoyol, you're really something!)

2096
01:30:06,356 --> 01:30:08,324
Come on, guys, block well!

2097
01:30:08,825 --> 01:30:09,691
Time out.

2098
01:30:13,563 --> 01:30:17,032
Suwon Special City calls
its second timeout.

2099
01:30:27,744 --> 01:30:28,957
What do you think is our problem?

2100
01:30:29,980 --> 01:30:31,614
What do you think?

2101
01:30:35,295 --> 01:30:37,863
Giving instructions
from off the court is my job,

2102
01:30:37,888 --> 01:30:42,158
but it's you who have to work it out
on the court.

2103
01:30:42,159 --> 01:30:42,960
- Right.
- Right.

2104
01:30:42,960 --> 01:30:44,894
It's not like I can play with you
on the court.

2105
01:30:45,762 --> 01:30:46,795
Yeon Jae.

2106
01:30:46,796 --> 01:30:48,964
(Throughout the game,
he kept emphasizing it to Yeon Jae,)

2107
01:30:50,033 --> 01:30:54,637
(but the straight attacks weren't
executed.)

2108
01:30:55,705 --> 01:30:58,741
(They need Yeon Jae's straight shots.)

2109
01:30:59,776 --> 01:31:02,010
Position your blocks more precisely.

2110
01:31:02,012 --> 01:31:04,480
Handle the high balls coming in
closer to the line.

2111
01:31:04,481 --> 01:31:09,719
Defend against Yeon Jae's straight
with a high ball.

2112
01:31:09,719 --> 01:31:12,754
If it drops this way,
the defense can handle it.

2113
01:31:13,156 --> 01:31:14,423
- In 1, 2, 3.
- Let's go!

2114
01:31:14,424 --> 01:31:15,758
Let's go for it!

2115
01:31:15,759 --> 01:31:17,360
Make it count. Hit harder.

2116
01:31:17,360 --> 01:31:19,695
- Be more decisive.
- Okay.

2117
01:31:20,163 --> 01:31:24,033
(Second set, Suwon Special City 6
: Wonder Dogs 13)

2118
01:31:27,537 --> 01:31:29,371
Hit it.

2119
01:31:31,507 --> 01:31:35,110
(Stop Yeon Jae's straight attack.)

2120
01:31:41,651 --> 01:31:43,452
(Block failure)

2121
01:31:43,693 --> 01:31:45,694
(Frustrated)

2122
01:31:47,611 --> 01:31:49,011
The score is 13 to 7.

2123
01:31:52,829 --> 01:31:53,595
Mine.

2124
01:31:54,598 --> 01:31:56,265
- Set it!
- Set it.

2125
01:31:56,399 --> 01:31:57,265
In 1, 2!

2126
01:31:57,601 --> 01:31:59,735
Enkhsoyol sent the ball over
using her fist.

2127
01:31:59,736 --> 01:32:00,636
Right!
A back toss.

2128
01:32:03,039 --> 01:32:03,939
(They blocked it.)

2129
01:32:04,808 --> 01:32:05,641
Yeon Jae!

2130
01:32:06,201 --> 01:32:07,067
Toward Yeon Jae.

2131
01:32:07,410 --> 01:32:08,710
Open spike!

2132
01:32:09,513 --> 01:32:11,747
It's in.

2133
01:32:12,349 --> 01:32:14,650
(Two consecutive points lost
due to blocking errors.)

2134
01:32:15,152 --> 01:32:16,085
It's my mistake.

2135
01:32:16,110 --> 01:32:18,178
- Where did you catch it?
- It hit my right hand.

2136
01:32:20,023 --> 01:32:23,726
Suwon Special City isn't
an easy team to face.

2137
01:32:24,474 --> 01:32:28,011
Coach Kim calls a timeout immediately
to stop the opponent's run.

2138
01:32:28,036 --> 01:32:30,161
(The Wonder Dogs' timeout)

2139
01:32:30,582 --> 01:32:33,084
Do not play carelessly
in this kind of situation.

2140
01:32:33,085 --> 01:32:34,795
Where did I tell you
to handle the high ball?

2141
01:32:34,820 --> 01:32:36,487
You said to keep it on the left hand.
I said left hand,

2142
01:32:36,488 --> 01:32:37,690
so why did you use the right?

2143
01:32:37,690 --> 01:32:39,122
That was an easy situation.

2144
01:32:39,124 --> 01:32:42,226
When a high ball comes in,
use your left hand to direct it straight.

2145
01:32:42,227 --> 01:32:44,195
Keep this in mind.

2146
01:32:44,529 --> 01:32:46,196
(But in the previous play,)

2147
01:32:46,198 --> 01:32:48,900
(The ball hit her right hand.)

2148
01:32:50,476 --> 01:32:52,911
It wasn't a strong shot, but a soft tap.

2149
01:32:52,971 --> 01:32:54,838
Your positioning was right.
You could've handled it.

2150
01:32:54,839 --> 01:32:56,546
- Get your positions right.
- Let's do it again.

2151
01:32:56,808 --> 01:32:58,442
- In 1, 2, 3.
- Let's go!

2152
01:32:59,010 --> 01:33:00,711
We need to focus on the receive first.

2153
01:33:00,712 --> 01:33:01,812
Okay.

2154
01:33:03,982 --> 01:33:05,649
Enkhsoyol!

2155
01:33:05,951 --> 01:33:08,251
If they block your feint,
what should you do?

2156
01:33:08,253 --> 01:33:09,587
Then, a spike.

2157
01:33:11,389 --> 01:33:13,256
Right. Hit it hard.

2158
01:33:13,925 --> 01:33:16,661
(Second set, Suwon Special City 8
: Wonder Dogs 13)

2159
01:33:16,728 --> 01:33:18,293
Watch out for a floater serve!

2160
01:33:20,966 --> 01:33:22,300
The receive is off.

2161
01:33:23,101 --> 01:33:24,935
(Straight to Enkhsoyol)

2162
01:33:25,904 --> 01:33:27,838
(They saved the spike.)

2163
01:33:29,474 --> 01:33:30,707
She's going for the ball!

2164
01:33:30,709 --> 01:33:31,876
(The ball goes to Yeon Jae again.)

2165
01:33:33,411 --> 01:33:34,978
(Their block is broken.)

2166
01:33:37,115 --> 01:33:38,215
Hye In's dig!

2167
01:33:38,450 --> 01:33:39,950
And Sol too!

2168
01:33:41,653 --> 01:33:42,987
(They handled the soft tip easily.)

2169
01:33:44,055 --> 01:33:45,022
Spike.

2170
01:33:49,361 --> 01:33:50,661
- Hye In!
- What a nice dig.

2171
01:33:50,662 --> 01:33:52,029
The ball is alive!

2172
01:33:53,598 --> 01:33:54,464
Enkhsoyol!

2173
01:33:55,767 --> 01:33:57,001
Attack coverage again!

2174
01:33:57,002 --> 01:33:59,036
Send it in!

2175
01:34:00,438 --> 01:34:02,853
(The soft tip attack keeps
getting blocked.)

2176
01:34:03,041 --> 01:34:03,841
Hyeon Jeong.

2177
01:34:04,242 --> 01:34:06,343
They are defending tenaciously.

2178
01:34:06,978 --> 01:34:08,512
The rally is getting longer.

2179
01:34:10,315 --> 01:34:11,148
Block along the line.

2180
01:34:12,551 --> 01:34:13,451
The spike is blocked.

2181
01:34:13,585 --> 01:34:14,451
Great!

2182
01:34:18,056 --> 01:34:20,057
A soft tip! But they kept it alive!

2183
01:34:21,293 --> 01:34:23,628
(We must end the rally here.)

2184
01:34:23,929 --> 01:34:26,097
(What if a tip doesn't work?)

2185
01:34:26,097 --> 01:34:29,099
I must hit it hard.

2186
01:34:30,669 --> 01:34:32,737
(Enkhsoyol scores with a spike.)

2187
01:34:32,737 --> 01:34:36,139
Enkhsoyol! The ball drops inside.

2188
01:34:36,140 --> 01:34:38,141
They take this rally.

2189
01:34:38,643 --> 01:34:40,277
(Enkhsoyol is not only capable
of tipping into Zone Three!)

2190
01:34:40,278 --> 01:34:41,211
That's it!

2191
01:34:41,212 --> 01:34:42,646
(She is strong too!)

2192
01:34:42,647 --> 01:34:43,413
(Coughing)

2193
01:34:43,982 --> 01:34:45,916
Enkhsoyol...

2194
01:34:47,052 --> 01:34:48,652
(Suddenly calming down)

2195
01:34:48,653 --> 01:34:50,153
Great job. Hit it like that.

2196
01:34:50,722 --> 01:34:52,623
Do not hesitate.

2197
01:34:52,791 --> 01:34:54,825
The Wonder Dogs are not only strong
at blocking,

2198
01:34:54,826 --> 01:34:56,593
they also dig difficult balls...

2199
01:34:57,229 --> 01:34:59,463
with their defense.

2200
01:34:59,464 --> 01:35:02,399
Their commitment to the ball
is outstanding.

2201
01:35:02,400 --> 01:35:07,137
Hye In and Myoung Hwa saved the ball
just before it hit the floor.

2202
01:35:07,305 --> 01:35:09,740
By digging persistently like this,

2203
01:35:09,741 --> 01:35:12,710
- they can wear down the opponents.
- Exactly.

2204
01:35:13,278 --> 01:35:14,625
Our coordination was excellent.

2205
01:35:14,913 --> 01:35:17,214
Everyone executed what we practiced...

2206
01:35:17,215 --> 01:35:20,584
exactly as we learned
in the video meeting.

2207
01:35:21,119 --> 01:35:23,452
Only now did it feel like
our play was really coming together,

2208
01:35:23,477 --> 01:35:26,657
and I thought we should keep it this way.

2209
01:35:28,193 --> 01:35:30,916
Enkhsoyol is getting more solid
as the game goes on.

2210
01:35:31,810 --> 01:35:33,374
(Keep this up.)

2211
01:35:33,494 --> 01:35:34,561
Serve!

2212
01:35:37,374 --> 01:35:38,407
No!

2213
01:35:41,507 --> 01:35:44,407
(Enkhsoyol's ball is out.)

2214
01:35:47,341 --> 01:35:48,341
That girl.

2215
01:35:49,474 --> 01:35:51,107
(Shoot.)

2216
01:35:51,607 --> 01:35:53,007
My mistake. Catch the ball first!

2217
01:35:53,007 --> 01:35:54,374
(Getting solid)

2218
01:35:56,241 --> 01:35:59,141
(Second set, Suwon Special City 10:
Wonder Dogs 16)

2219
01:35:59,184 --> 01:36:00,217
Serve!

2220
01:36:00,242 --> 01:36:01,375
In 1, 2!

2221
01:36:01,400 --> 01:36:02,800
- Mine!
- Sorry!

2222
01:36:03,241 --> 01:36:04,274
Sorry!

2223
01:36:05,541 --> 01:36:06,907
Han Song Hee saved the ball.

2224
01:36:08,107 --> 01:36:10,074
(Suwon Special City's free ball)

2225
01:36:10,574 --> 01:36:11,641
The short hit is blocked.

2226
01:36:12,041 --> 01:36:13,141
They dug it.

2227
01:36:13,674 --> 01:36:14,707
To the right.

2228
01:36:16,707 --> 01:36:17,874
They score with a touch out!

2229
01:36:17,874 --> 01:36:19,107
(A block touch out)

2230
01:36:19,107 --> 01:36:20,741
- We did it.
- Thank you!

2231
01:36:20,741 --> 01:36:24,174
Even if a player makes an error,

2232
01:36:24,174 --> 01:36:27,774
another is giving all she's got
to make coverage.

2233
01:36:27,774 --> 01:36:28,774
I know, right?

2234
01:36:28,774 --> 01:36:31,207
That's how teamwork is made.

2235
01:36:31,741 --> 01:36:33,407
It's 17 to 10.

2236
01:36:34,207 --> 01:36:35,274
Moon Myoung Hwa is out.

2237
01:36:35,274 --> 01:36:37,674
And Back Chae Rim is in to serve.

2238
01:36:41,141 --> 01:36:43,641
(Today, Chae Rim isn't the number 8
of Suwon Special City.)

2239
01:36:43,641 --> 01:36:46,741
(She is number 8 of the Wonder Dogs.)

2240
01:36:46,941 --> 01:36:48,970
She can't keep tilting her head.

2241
01:36:49,774 --> 01:36:52,574
(Are you here to tilt your head?)

2242
01:36:52,574 --> 01:36:53,874
(Glaring)

2243
01:36:56,207 --> 01:36:58,341
(To number 1)

2244
01:37:00,707 --> 01:37:01,974
Nice serve!

2245
01:37:05,707 --> 01:37:06,807
(It worked.)

2246
01:37:08,874 --> 01:37:10,274
The reception is shaken.

2247
01:37:10,274 --> 01:37:11,807
(Chae Rim's serve shook their reception.)

2248
01:37:11,807 --> 01:37:13,307
Nice. Push it!

2249
01:37:13,774 --> 01:37:15,074
Set it up!

2250
01:37:15,641 --> 01:37:18,107
(Kim Na Hee moves to the center
after hearing Chae Rim.)

2251
01:37:18,741 --> 01:37:19,807
Koo Sol!

2252
01:37:19,807 --> 01:37:21,774
- Nice play!
- Kim Na Hee!

2253
01:37:21,774 --> 01:37:23,807
- So nice!
- Nice!

2254
01:37:25,274 --> 01:37:27,407
It was their first quick attack.

2255
01:37:27,407 --> 01:37:31,007
We saw a player preparing for a quick
for the first time.

2256
01:37:31,007 --> 01:37:33,741
If there's a huge gap
and the team gets a chance,

2257
01:37:33,741 --> 01:37:35,474
it's better to play boldly like this.

2258
01:37:35,474 --> 01:37:36,541
You're right.

2259
01:37:37,107 --> 01:37:39,307
(Former Suwon Special City players
did it!)

2260
01:37:39,707 --> 01:37:40,941
Chae Rim!

2261
01:37:40,941 --> 01:37:43,007
(Good job.)

2262
01:37:43,407 --> 01:37:44,707
(Feeling conflicted)

2263
01:37:44,707 --> 01:37:45,926
Nice. Keep this up.

2264
01:37:46,607 --> 01:37:48,874
(Back Chae Rim serves again.)

2265
01:37:51,874 --> 01:37:54,674
(It's a quick attack this time!)

2266
01:37:56,441 --> 01:38:00,807
(Na Hee has been preparing
for Suwon Special City's quick.)

2267
01:38:05,874 --> 01:38:06,941
(Na Hee scores with a block.)

2268
01:38:06,941 --> 01:38:09,307
She blocked it!

2269
01:38:09,307 --> 01:38:11,207
- So nice!
- Nice!

2270
01:38:11,207 --> 01:38:12,374
(Nice one again, Na Hee!)

2271
01:38:12,941 --> 01:38:14,607
After launching a quick by herself,

2272
01:38:14,607 --> 01:38:17,241
Na Hee guards the zone...

2273
01:38:17,241 --> 01:38:19,241
as she knows her opponents well.

2274
01:38:19,241 --> 01:38:21,007
A perfect block to score!

2275
01:38:21,007 --> 01:38:23,441
(Kim Na Hee, Number 7 of the Wonder Dogs)

2276
01:38:27,141 --> 01:38:30,074
(The Wonder Dogs seize the clear lead.)

2277
01:38:32,641 --> 01:38:33,807
Keep this up.

2278
01:38:33,807 --> 01:38:38,341
(Know yourself and your opponents.
That's how you'll never lose.)

2279
01:38:38,541 --> 01:38:40,907
Great work, Na Hee.

2280
01:38:41,374 --> 01:38:42,641
It's 19 to 10.

2281
01:38:42,641 --> 01:38:44,941
The Wonder Dogs are ahead by nine points.

2282
01:38:46,485 --> 01:38:48,952
(A head-to-head battle
against their former team)

2283
01:38:48,952 --> 01:38:51,118
(I will read what you have in mind.)

2284
01:38:51,118 --> 01:38:52,118
(Like a father,)

2285
01:38:52,585 --> 01:38:55,385
(I'll not go easy on you.)

2286
01:38:55,618 --> 01:38:57,852
(The rookie coach is on the edge.)

2287
01:38:58,285 --> 01:38:59,718
(And Captain Pyo's former club)

2288
01:38:59,985 --> 01:39:02,151
(The former team that knows me too much)

2289
01:39:02,851 --> 01:39:06,151
(A truly tough rally)

2290
01:39:08,785 --> 01:39:10,751
(Feeling like running away)

2291
01:39:10,751 --> 01:39:13,518
What's scaring you?

2292
01:39:13,518 --> 01:39:14,751
Go one by one.

2293
01:39:17,018 --> 01:39:18,051
(They received it...)

2294
01:39:18,051 --> 01:39:19,285
(and set it up well.)

2295
01:39:19,651 --> 01:39:21,585
(Now, it's time to hit hard!)

2296
01:39:24,851 --> 01:39:27,185
(The red wall of a pro team)

2297
01:39:27,651 --> 01:39:29,851
(Can the Wonder Dogs break through it?)

2298
01:39:29,851 --> 01:39:31,485
The answer is right there!
